DG.put("krisnaavtaar/28",{"n":28,"title":"ਅਥ ਕੁੰਜ ਗਲੀਨ ਮੈ ਖੇਲਬੋ","title_roman":"Ath kunj galeen mai khelbo","page":437,"blocks":[{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":437,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[649],"number_text":"੬੪੯।","page":437,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਰਿ ਕੈ ਤਾਹਿ ਕਿਧੌ ਮੁਸਲੀ ਹਰਿ ਬੰਸੀ ਬਜਾਈ ਨ ਕੈ ਕਛੁ ਸੰਕਾ।","roman":"Maari kai taahi kidhau muslee hari bansee bajaaee na kai kachhu sankaa |","meaning_en":"Having slain him, Balram and Krishna played the flute without the least fear;","page":437,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮੁਸਲੀ: 'the pestle-bearer', i.e. Balram; 'ਮੁਸਲੀ ਹਰਿ' could also be read as one epithet of Krishna; uncertain. 'him' = the foe slain in the preceding episode."},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਵਨ ਖੇਤ ਮਰਿਯੋ ਕੁਪ ਕੈ ਜਿਨਿ ਰੀਝਿ ਬਿਭੀਛਨ ਦੀਨ ਸੁ ਲੰਕਾ।","roman":"Raavan khet mariyo kup kai jini reejhi bibheechhan deen su lankaa |","meaning_en":"he who in anger slew Ravan on the battlefield, and, well pleased, gave Lanka to Vibhishan;","page":437,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾ ਕੋ ਲਖਿਯੋ ਕੁਬਜਾ ਬਲ ਬਾਹਨ ਜਾ ਕੋ ਲਖਿਯੋ ਮੁਰ ਦੈਤ ਅਤੰਕਾ।","roman":"Jaa ko lakhiyo kubjaa bal baahan jaa ko lakhiyo mur dait atankaa |","meaning_en":"he whom Kubja saw as her strength and support, he whom the demon Mur saw as terror —","page":437,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਲ ਬਾਹਨ: read as 'strength and support'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੀਝਿ ਬਜਾਇ ਉਠਿਯੋ ਮੁਰਲੀ ਸੋਈ ਜੀਤ ਦੀਯੋ ਜਸੁ ਕੋ ਮਨੋ ਡੰਕਾ। ੬੪੯।","roman":"Reejhi bajaai uthiyo murlee soee jeet deeyo jasu ko mano dankaa | 649 |","meaning_en":"that same one rose in delight and played the flute, as though beating the drum of victory and glory.","page":437,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[650],"number_text":"੬੫੦।","page":438,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰੂਖਨ ਤੇ ਰਸ ਚੂਵਨ ਲਾਗ ਝਰੈ ਝਰਨਾ ਗਿਰਿ ਤੇ ਸੁਖਦਾਈ।","roman":"Rookhan te ras choovan laag jharai jharnaa giri te sukhdaaee |","meaning_en":"Sap began to drip from the trees, and pleasant springs poured down from the hills;","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਘਾਸ ਚੁਗੈ ਨ ਮ੍ਰਿਗਾ ਬਨ ਕੇ ਖਗ ਰੀਝ ਰਹੇ ਧੁਨਿ ਜਾ ਸੁਨਿ ਪਾਈ।","roman":"Ghaas chugai na mrigaa ban ke khag reejh rahe dhuni jaa suni paaee |","meaning_en":"the deer of the forest stopped grazing, and the birds that heard the sound were enchanted;","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਵ ਗੰਧਾਰਿ ਬਿਲਾਵਲ ਸਾਰੰਗ ਕੀ ਰਿਝ ਕੈ ਜਿਹ ਤਾਨ ਬਸਾਈ।","roman":"Dev gandhaari bilaaval saarang kee rijh kai jih taan basaaee |","meaning_en":"he who, delighted, set ringing the strains of Dev Gandhari, Bilawal and Sarang —","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Names of ragas."},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਵ ਸਭੈ ਮਿਲਿ ਦੇਖਤ ਕਉਤਕ ਜਉ ਮੁਰਲੀ ਨੰਦ ਲਾਲ ਬਜਾਈ। ੬੫੦।","roman":"Dev sabhai mili dekhat kautak jau murlee nand laal bajaaee | 650 |","meaning_en":"all the gods gathered to watch the wonder when Nand's darling played the flute.","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[651],"number_text":"੬੫੧।","page":438,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਠਾਢ ਰਹੀ ਜਮੁਨਾ ਸੁਨਿ ਕੈ ਧੁਨਿ ਰਾਗ ਭਲੇ ਸੁਨਬੇ ਕੋ ਚਹੇ ਹੈ।","roman":"Thaadh rahee jamunaa suni kai dhuni raag bhale sunbe ko chahe hai |","meaning_en":"The Yamuna stood still on hearing the sound, longing to hear the lovely ragas;","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੋਹਿ ਰਹੇ ਬਨ ਕੇ ਗਜ ਅਉ ਮ੍ਰਿਗ ਇਕਠੇ ਮਿਲਿ ਆਵਤ ਸਿੰਘ ਸਹੇ ਹੈ।","roman":"Mohi rahe ban ke gaj au mrig ikthe mili aavat singh sahe hai |","meaning_en":"the elephants and deer of the forest were spellbound, and lions came along together with hares;","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਹੇ: read as 'hares'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਵਤ ਹੈ ਸੁਰ ਮੰਡਲ ਕੇ ਸੁਰ ਤ੍ਯਾਗਿ ਸਭੈ ਸੁਰ ਧ੍ਯਾਨ ਫਹੇ ਹੈ।","roman":"Aavat hai sur mandal ke sur tyaagi sabhai sur dhyaan phahe hai |","meaning_en":"the gods of the heavenly realm came, all the gods leaving (their places), caught up in rapt attention;","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁਰ ਤ੍ਯਾਗਿ: 'leaving (their places)'; could mean 'leaving their own music'. ਫਹੇ: 'caught, ensnared'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋ ਸੁਨਿ ਕੈ ਬਨ ਕੇ ਖਗਵਾ ਤਰੁ ਊਪਰ ਪੰਖ ਪਸਾਰਿ ਰਹੇ ਹੈ। ੬੫੧।","roman":"So suni kai ban ke khagvaa taru oopar pankh pasaari rahe hai | 651 |","meaning_en":"hearing it, the birds of the forest stayed on the trees with their wings spread.","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[652],"number_text":"੬੫੨।","page":438,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋਊ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਖੇਲਤ ਹੈ ਹਰਿ ਸੋ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਹਿਤ ਕੈ ਨ ਕਛੂ ਧਨ ਮੈ।","roman":"Jo'oo gvaarin khelat hai hari so ati hee hit kai na kachhoo dhan mai |","meaning_en":"The gopis who play with Krishna with great love, caring nothing for wealth,","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨ ਕਛੂ ਧਨ ਮੈ: read as 'caring nothing for wealth'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਪੈ ਜਿਹ ਬੀਚ ਲਸੈ ਫੁਨਿ ਕੰਚਨ ਕੀ ਸੁ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਤਨ ਮੈ।","roman":"Ati sundar pai jih beech lasai phuni kanchan kee su prabhaa tan mai |","meaning_en":"very beautiful, in whose bodies shines the radiance of gold;","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋਊ ਚੰਦ੍ਰਮੁਖੀ ਕਟਿ ਕੇਹਰਿ ਸੀ ਸੁ ਬਿਰਾਜਤ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਕੇ ਗਨ ਮੈ।","roman":"Jo'oo chandramukhee kati kehri see su biraajat gvaarin ke gan mai |","meaning_en":"moon-faced, lion-waisted, who sit resplendent in the company of gopis —","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨਿ ਕੈ ਮੁਰਲੀ ਧੁਨਿ ਸ੍ਰਉਨਨ ਮੈ ਅਤਿ ਰੀਝਿ ਗਿਰੀ ਸੁ ਮਨੋ ਬਨ ਮੈ। ੬੫੨।","roman":"Suni kai murlee dhuni sraunan mai ati reejhi giree su mano ban mai | 652 |","meaning_en":"hearing the sound of the flute in their ears, they fell down in the forest, utterly enraptured.","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[653],"number_text":"੬੫੩।","page":438,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਹ ਕਉਤੁਕ ਕੈ ਸੁ ਚਲੇ ਗ੍ਰਿਹ ਕੇ ਫੁਨਿ ਗਾਵਤ ਗੀਤ ਹਲੀ ਹਰਿ ਆਛੇ।","roman":"Ih kautuk kai su chale grih ke phuni gaavat geet halee hari aachhe |","meaning_en":"Having done this wonder, the fine pair, Balram and Krishna, set off for home singing songs;","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹਲੀ: 'the plough-bearer', Balram."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁੰਦਰ ਬੀਚ ਅਖਾਰੇ ਕਿਧੌ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਨਟੂਆ ਜਨੁ ਕਾਛੇ।","roman":"Sundar beech akhaare kidhau kabi syaam kahai natooaa janu kaachhe |","meaning_en":"the poet Shyam says, they look like actors in costume in a beautiful arena;","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਜਤ ਹੈ ਬਲਭਦ੍ਰ ਕੇ ਨੈਨ ਯੌ ਮਾਨੋ ਢਰੇ ਇਹ ਮੈਨ ਕੇ ਸਾਛੇ।","roman":"Raajat hai balbhadr ke nain yau maano dhare ih main ke saachhe |","meaning_en":"Balbhadra's eyes shine as if they were cast in the mould of Kamdev;","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Balbhadra = Balram."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁੰਦਰ ਹੈ ਰਤਿ ਕੇ ਪਤਿ ਤੈ ਅਤਿ ਮਾਨਹੁ ਡਾਰਤ ਮੈਨਹਿ ਪਾਛੇ। ੬੫੩।","roman":"Sundar hai rati ke pati tai ati maanhu daarat mainhi paachhe | 653 |","meaning_en":"they are more beautiful than Rati's husband, as if leaving Kamdev behind.","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[654],"number_text":"੬੫੪।","page":438,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬੀਚ ਮਨੈ ਸੁਖ ਪਾਇ ਤਬੈ ਗ੍ਰਿਹ ਕੌ ਸੁ ਚਲੇ ਰਿਪੁ ਕੌ ਹਨਿ ਦੋਊ।","roman":"Beech manai sukh paai tabai grih kau su chale ripu kau hani do'oo |","meaning_en":"Then, glad at heart, the two set off for home having slain the foe;","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚੰਦ੍ਰਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਸਮ ਜਾ ਮੁਖ ਉਪਮਾ ਜਾ ਸਮ ਉਪਮ ਹੈ ਨਹਿ ਕੋਊ।","roman":"Chandraprabhaa sam jaa mukh upmaa jaa sam upam hai nahi ko'oo |","meaning_en":"their faces are likened to moonlight, and none can be likened to them;","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਖਤ ਰੀਝ ਰਹੈ ਜਿਹ ਕੋ ਰਿਪੁ ਰੀਝਤ ਸੋਇ ਨ ਦੇਖਤ ਸੋਊ।","roman":"Dekhat reejh rahai jih ko ripu reejhat soi na dekhat so'oo |","meaning_en":"seeing them, even the foe is charmed; whoever is not charmed is one who has not seen them;","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Second half read loosely; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਨਹੁ ਲਛਮਨ ਰਾਮ ਬਡੇ ਭਟ ਮਾਰਿ ਚਲੇ ਰਿਪੁ ਕੋ ਘਰ ਓਊ। ੬੫੪।","roman":"Maanhu lachhman raam bade bhat maari chale ripu ko ghar o'oo | 654 |","meaning_en":"as if the great warriors Lakshman and Ram were going home after slaying the enemy.","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"section_heading","name":"ਅਥ ਕੁੰਜ ਗਲੀਨ ਮੈ ਖੇਲਬੋ","gurmukhi":"ਅਥ ਕੁੰਜ ਗਲੀਨ ਮੈ ਖੇਲਬੋ","roman":"Ath kunj galeen mai khelbo","meaning_en":"Now begins the play in the arbour lanes.","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[655],"number_text":"੬੫੫।","page":438,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਰਿ ਸੰਗਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਇਮ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਕੇ ਅਬ ਕੁੰਜ ਗਲੀਨ ਮੈ ਖੇਲ ਮਚਈਯੈ।","roman":"Hari sangi kahiyo im gvaarin ke ab kunj galeen mai khel machaeeyai |","meaning_en":"Krishna spoke thus to the gopis: 'Now let us start play in the arbour lanes;","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਾਚਤ ਖੇਲਤ ਭਾਤਿ ਭਲੀ ਸੁ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਯੌ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਗੀਤ ਬਸਈਯੈ।","roman":"Naachat khelat bhaati bhalee su kahiyo yau sundar geet basaeeyai |","meaning_en":"dancing and playing in fine style,' he said, 'let us make beautiful songs resound;","page":438,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾ ਕੇ ਹੀਏ ਮਨੁ ਹੋਤ ਖੁਸ਼ੀ ਸੁਨੀਯੈ ਉਠਿ ਕੇ ਸੋਊ ਕਾਰਜ ਕਈਯੈ।","roman":"Jaa ke hee'e manu hot khushee suneeyai uthi ke so'oo kaaraj kaeeyai |","meaning_en":"listen: whatever makes the heart glad, let us rise and do that very thing;","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੀਰ ਨਦੀ ਹਮਰੀ ਸਿਖ ਲੈ ਸੁਖ ਆਪਨ ਦੈ ਹਮ ਹੂੰ ਸੁਖ ਦਈਯੈ। ੬੫੫।","roman":"Teer nadee hamree sikh lai sukh aapan dai ham hoon sukh daeeyai | 655 |","meaning_en":"on the river bank, take my counsel: give me joy, and I will give you joy too.'","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[656],"number_text":"੬੫੬।","page":439,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਕੋ ਆਇਸੁ ਮਾਨਿ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਕੁੰਜ ਗਲੀਨ ਮੈ ਖੇਲ ਮਚਾਯੋ।","roman":"Kaanh ko aaisu maani treeyaa brij kunj galeen mai khel machaayo |","meaning_en":"Obeying Krishna's command, the women of Braj began play in the arbour lanes;","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਾਇ ਉਠੀ ਸੋਊ ਗੀਤ ਭਲੀ ਬਿਧਿ ਜੋ ਹਰਿ ਕੇ ਮਨ ਭੀਤਰ ਭਾਯੋ।","roman":"Gaai uthee so'oo geet bhalee bidhi jo hari ke man bheetar bhaayo |","meaning_en":"they sang well the very songs that pleased Krishna's heart;","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਵ ਗੰਧਾਰਿ ਅਉ ਸੁਧ ਮਲਾਰ ਬਿਖੈ ਸੋਊ ਭਾਖਿ ਖਿਆਲ ਬਸਾਯੋ।","roman":"Dev gandhaari au sudh malaar bikhai so'oo bhaakhi khiaal basaayo |","meaning_en":"in Dev Gandhari and pure Malar they sang, setting out the khayal;","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਖਿਆਲ: read as the khayal style of singing; could mean 'melody/thought'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੀਝ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਪੁਰਿ ਮੰਡਲ ਅਉ ਸੁਰ ਮੰਡਲ ਪੈ ਜਿਨ ਹੂੰ ਸੁਨਿ ਪਾਯੋ। ੬੫੬।","roman":"Reejh rahiyo puri mandal au sur mandal pai jin hoon suni paayo | 656 |","meaning_en":"those in the town and in the realm of the gods who heard it were enraptured.","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[657],"number_text":"੬੫੭।","page":439,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਸਿਰ ਪੈ ਧਰ ਕੈ ਮਿਲਿ ਕੁੰਜਨ ਮੈ ਸੁਭ ਭਾਤਿ ਗਈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Kaanh kahiyo sir pai dhar kai mili kunjan mai subh bhaati gaee hai |","meaning_en":"Taking Krishna's word upon their heads, they went together, in fine manner, into the arbours;","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੰਜ ਮੁਖੀ ਤਨ ਕੰਚਨ ਸੇ ਸਭ ਰੂਪ ਬਿਖੈ ਮਨੋ ਮੈਨ ਮਈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Kanj mukhee tan kanchan se sabh roop bikhai mano main maee hai |","meaning_en":"lotus-faced and golden-bodied, all as if made of Kamdev himself in beauty;","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਖੇਲ ਬਿਖੈ ਰਸ ਕੀ ਸੋ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਸਭ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕੇ ਆਗੇ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਐਸੇ ਧਈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Khel bikhai ras kee so treeyaa sabh syaam ke aage hvai aise dhaee hai |","meaning_en":"in the play all those women, full of love's delight, ran ahead of Shyam thus;","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਉਪਮਾ ਗਜ ਗਾਮਨਿ ਕਾਮਿਨ ਰੂਪ ਭਈ ਹੈ। ੬੫੭।","roman":"Yau kabi syaam kahai upmaa gaj gaamni kaamin roop bhaee hai | 657 |","meaning_en":"the poet Shyam gives this likeness: the women with an elephant's gait became the very form of passion.","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[658],"number_text":"੬੫੮।","page":439,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਛੁਹਿਯੋ ਚਹੈ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਕੌ ਸੋਊ ਭਾਗ ਚਲੈ ਨਹੀ ਦੇਤ ਛੁਹਾਈ।","roman":"Kaanh chhuhiyo chahai gvaarin kau so'oo bhaag chalai nahee det chhuhaaee |","meaning_en":"Kanh wants to touch the gopis; they run away and do not let themselves be touched,","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਉ ਮ੍ਰਿਗਨੀ ਅਪਨੇ ਪਤਿ ਕੋ ਰਤਿ ਕੇਲ ਸਮੈ ਨਹੀ ਦੇਤ ਮਿਲਾਈ।","roman":"Jiu mrignee apne pati ko rati kel samai nahee det milaaee |","meaning_en":"as a doe does not let her mate come near her at the time of love-play;","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੁੰਜਨ ਭੀਤਰ ਤੀਰ ਨਦੀ ਬ੍ਰਿਖ ਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਸੁ ਫਿਰੈ ਤਹ ਧਾਈ।","roman":"Kunjan bheetar teer nadee brikh bhaan sutaa su phirai tah dhaaee |","meaning_en":"within the arbours on the river bank, Brikhbhan's daughter runs about there;","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Brikhbhan's daughter = Radha."},{"gurmukhi":"ਠਉਰ ਤਹਾ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਸੋ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਜੂ ਖੇਲ ਮਚਾਈ। ੬੫੮।","roman":"Thaur tahaa kabi syaam kahai ih bhaati so syaam joo khel machaaee | 658 |","meaning_en":"in that place, says the poet Shyam, Shyam set the play going in this way.","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"The poet's pen-name Shyam and Krishna's name Shyam both appear."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[659],"number_text":"੬੫੯।","page":439,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਤਿ ਕਰੀ ਛਠ ਮਾਸਨ ਕੀ ਅਤਿ ਉਜਲ ਪੈ ਸੋਊ ਅਰਧ ਅੰਧੇਰੀ।","roman":"Raati karee chhath maasan kee ati ujal pai so'oo aradh andheree |","meaning_en":"He made the night as long as six months, very bright and yet half dark;","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Read as the night being lengthened to six months; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਸਮੈ ਤਿਹ ਠਉਰ ਬਿਖੈ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਸਭੈ ਹਰਿ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਘੇਰੀ।","roman":"Taahee samai tih thaur bikhai kabi syaam sabhai hari gvaarin gheree |","meaning_en":"at that time, in that place, says the poet Shyam, Krishna surrounded all the gopis;","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨੈਨ ਕੀ ਕੋਰ ਕਟਾਛਨ ਪੇਖਤ ਝੂਮਿ ਗਿਰੀ ਇਕ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਗਈ ਚੇਰੀ।","roman":"Nain kee kor kataachhan pekhat jhoomi giree ik hvai gaee cheree |","meaning_en":"seeing the side-glances from the corners of his eyes, one swooned and fell and became his servant;","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਉਪਜੀ ਉਪਮਾ ਜੀਯ ਮੈ ਸਰ ਸੋ ਮ੍ਰਿਗਨੀ ਜਿਮ ਘਾਵਤ ਹੇਰੀ। ੬੫੯।","roman":"Yau upjee upmaa jeey mai sar so mrignee jim ghaavat heree | 659 |","meaning_en":"this likeness arose in the mind: like a doe seen wounded by an arrow.","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[660],"number_text":"੬੬੦।","page":439,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਫੇਰ ਉਠੈ ਉਠਤੇ ਹੀ ਭਗੈ ਜਦੁਰਾ ਕੌ ਨ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਦੇਤ ਮਿਲਾਈ।","roman":"Pher uthai uthte hee bhagai jaduraa kau na gvaarin det milaaee |","meaning_en":"She rises again and, as soon as she rises, runs; the gopis do not let the Yadav king reach them;","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜਦੁਰਾ / ਜਦੁਰਾਇ: 'king of the Yadavs', Krishna."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਛੈ ਪਰੈ ਤਿਨ ਕੇ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਚੜਿ ਕੈ ਰਸ ਕੈ ਹਯ ਊਪਰ ਧਾਈ।","roman":"Paachhai parai tin ke hari joo chari kai ras kai hay oopar dhaaee |","meaning_en":"Krishna follows after them, as if mounted on the horse of love and galloping;","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਧੇ ਕੋ ਨੈਨਨ ਕੇ ਸਰ ਸੰਗ ਬਧੈ ਮਨੋ ਭਉਹ ਕਮਾਨ ਚੜਾਈ।","roman":"Raadhe ko nainan ke sar sang badhai mano bhauh kamaan charaaee |","meaning_en":"he pierces Radha with the arrows of his eyes, as though drawing the bow of his brows;","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਝੂਮਿ ਗਿਰੈ ਧਰਨੀ ਪਰ ਸੋ ਮ੍ਰਿਗਨੀ ਮ੍ਰਿਗਹਾ ਮਨੋ ਮਾਰਿ ਗਿਰਾਈ। ੬੬੦।","roman":"Jhoomi girai dharnee par so mrignee mrighaa mano maari giraaee | 660 |","meaning_en":"she swoons and falls to the ground like a doe struck down by a hunter.","page":439,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[661],"number_text":"੬੬੧।","page":440,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਧਿ ਲੈ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨੁ ਸੁਤਾ ਤਬ ਹੀ ਹਰਿ ਅਗ੍ਰਜ ਕੁੰਜਨ ਮੈ ਉਠਿ ਭਾਗੈ।","roman":"Sudhi lai brikhbhaanu sutaa tab hee hari agraj kunjan mai uthi bhaagai |","meaning_en":"Coming to her senses, Brikhbhan's daughter at once rose and fled before Krishna into the arbours;","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਸ ਸੋ ਜਦੁਰਾਇ ਮਹਾ ਰਸੀਆ ਤਬ ਹੀ ਤਿਹ ਕੇ ਪਿਛੂਆਨ ਸੋ ਲਾਗੈ।","roman":"Ras so jaduraai mahaa raseeaa tab hee tih ke pichhooaan so laagai |","meaning_en":"and the Yadav king, the great lover, at once went after her with delight;","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੋਛ ਲਹੈ ਨਰ ਸੋ ਛਿਨ ਮੈ ਹਰਿ ਕੇ ਇਹ ਕਉਤੁਕ ਜੋ ਅਨੁਰਾਗੈ।","roman":"Mochh lahai nar so chhin mai hari ke ih kautuk jo anuraagai |","meaning_en":"the man who loves this play of Krishna gains liberation in an instant;","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਉਪਜੈ ਉਪਮਾ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਮ੍ਰਿਗਨੀ ਜਿਮ ਘਾਇਲ ਸ੍ਵਾਰ ਕੇ ਆਗੈ। ੬੬੧।","roman":"Yau upjai upmaa man mai mrignee jim ghaail svaar ke aagai | 661 |","meaning_en":"this likeness arises in the mind: like a wounded doe in front of a horseman.","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[662],"number_text":"੬੬੨।","page":440,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਭਾਗਤ ਕੁੰਜ ਗਲੀਨ ਬਿਖੈ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨੁ ਸੁਤਾ ਕੋ ਗਹੇ ਹਰਿ ਐਸੇ।","roman":"Ati bhaagat kunj galeen bikhai brikhbhaanu sutaa ko gahe hari aise |","meaning_en":"As she ran hard through the arbour lanes, Krishna caught Brikhbhan's daughter thus,","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੈਧੌ ਧਵਾਇ ਧਵਾਇ ਮਹਾ ਜਮੁਨਾ ਤਟਿ ਹਾਰਤ ਮਾਨਕ ਜੈਸੇ।","roman":"Kaidhau dhavaai dhavaai mahaa jamunaa tati haarat maanak jaise |","meaning_en":"as if, after running and running along the Yamuna bank, one recovered a lost ruby;","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹਾਰਤ ਮਾਨਕ: read as 'a lost ruby'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੈ ਚੜਿ ਕੈ ਰਸ ਹੈ ਮਨ ਨੈਨਨ ਭਉਹ ਤਨਾਇ ਕੈ ਮਾਰਤ ਲੈਸੇ।","roman":"Pai chari kai ras hai man nainan bhauh tanaai kai maarat laise |","meaning_en":"mounted on love, he strikes her heart with his eyes, bending the bow of his brows, and takes her;","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Line read loosely; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਉਪਜੀ ਉਪਮਾ ਜਿਮ ਸ੍ਵਾਰ ਮਨੋ ਜਿਤ ਲੇਤ ਮ੍ਰਿਗੀ ਕਹੁ ਜੈਸੇ। ੬੬੨।","roman":"Yau upjee upmaa jim svaar mano jit let mrigee kahu jaise | 662 |","meaning_en":"this likeness arose: as a horseman wins and captures a doe.","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[663],"number_text":"੬੬੩।","page":440,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਹਿ ਕੈ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨੁ ਸੁਤਾ ਜਦੁਰਾਇ ਜੂ ਬੋਲਤ ਤਾ ਸੰਗਿ ਅੰਮ੍ਰਿਤ ਬਾਨੀ।","roman":"Gahi kai brikhbhaanu sutaa jaduraai joo bolat taa sangi anmrit baanee |","meaning_en":"Having caught Brikhbhan's daughter, the Yadav king speaks nectar-sweet words to her:","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਗਤ ਕਾਹੇ ਕੇ ਹੇਤ ਸੁਨੋ ਹਮ ਹੂੰ ਤੇ ਤੂੰ ਕਿਉ ਸੁਨਿ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਰਾਨੀ।","roman":"Bhaagat kaahe ke het suno ham hoon te toon kiu suni gvaarin raanee |","meaning_en":"'Listen, why do you run from me? Listen, queen of the gopis;","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੰਜਮੁਖੀ ਤਨ ਕੰਚਨ ਸੋ ਹਮ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਮਨ ਕੀ ਸਭ ਬਾਤ ਪਛਾਨੀ।","roman":"Kanjmukhee tan kanchan so ham hvai man kee sabh baat pachhaanee |","meaning_en":"lotus-faced one, golden-bodied, I have recognised everything in your heart.'","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕੇ ਪ੍ਰੇਮ ਛਕੀ ਮਨਿ ਸੁੰਦਰਿ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਬਨਿ ਖੋਜਤ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਦਿਵਾਨੀ। ੬੬੩।","roman":"Syaam ke prem chhakee mani sundri hvai bani khojat syaam divaanee | 663 |","meaning_en":"The beauty, steeped in love for Shyam, had gone about the forest searching for him like one crazed.","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[664],"number_text":"੬੬੪।","page":440,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਪਿਖਿ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਕੋ ਨਿਹੁਰਾਇ ਕੈ ਨੀਚੇ ਰਹੀ ਅਖੀਆ।","roman":"Brikhbhaan sutaa pikhi gvaarin ko nihuraai kai neeche rahee akheeaa |","meaning_en":"Brikhbhan's daughter, seeing the gopis, bent her head and kept her eyes lowered,","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਨੋ ਯਾ ਮ੍ਰਿਗ ਭਾ ਸਭ ਛੀਨ ਲਈ ਕਿ ਮਨੋ ਇਹ ਕੰਜਨ ਕੀ ਪਖੀਆ।","roman":"Mano yaa mrig bhaa sabh chheen laee ki mano ih kanjan kee pakheeaa |","meaning_en":"as if those eyes had taken away all the deer's lustre, or were the petals of lotuses;","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪਖੀਆ: read as 'petals'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਮ ਅੰਮ੍ਰਿਤ ਕੀ ਹਸਿ ਕੈ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਯੌ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਹਰਿ ਕੇ ਸੰਗ ਹੈ ਅਖੀਆ।","roman":"Sam anmrit kee hasi kai treeyaa yau bateeyaa hari ke sang hai akheeaa |","meaning_en":"smiling, the woman spoke these nectar-like words to Krishna:","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਰਿ ਛਾਡਿ ਦੈ ਮੋਹਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਹਮ ਕੌ ਸੁ ਨਿਹਾਰਤ ਹੈ ਸਭ ਹੀ ਸਖੀਆ। ੬੬੪।","roman":"Hari chhaadi dai mohi kahiyo ham kau su nihaarat hai sabh hee sakheeaa | 664 |","meaning_en":"'Krishna, let me go,' she said; 'all the friends are watching us.'","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[665],"number_text":"੬੬੫।","page":440,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨ ਕੈ ਹਰਿ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਕੀ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਨਹੀ ਛੋਰਤ ਤੋ ਕੌ।","roman":"Sun kai hari gvaarin kee bateeyaa ih bhaati kahiyo nahee chhorat to kau |","meaning_en":"Hearing the gopi's words, Krishna said thus: 'I will not let you go;","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਖਤ ਹੈ ਤੋ ਕਹਾ ਭਯੋ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਪੈ ਇਨ ਤੇ ਕਛੂ ਸੰਕ ਨ ਮੋ ਕੌ।","roman":"Dekhat hai to kahaa bhayo gvaarin pai in te kachhoo sank na mo kau |","meaning_en":"what if they are watching, gopi? I have no fear of them at all;","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉ ਹਮਰੀ ਰਸ ਖੇਲਨ ਕੀ ਇਹ ਠਉਰ ਬਿਖੈ ਕੀ ਨਹੀ ਸੁਧਿ ਲੋਕੋ।","roman":"Au hamree ras khelan kee ih thaur bikhai kee nahee sudhi loko |","meaning_en":"and people know nothing of this place of our loving play;","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਹੇ ਕਉ ਮੋ ਸੋ ਬਿਬਾਦ ਕਰੈ ਸੁ ਡਰੈ ਇਨ ਤੇ ਬਿਨ ਹੀ ਸੁ ਤੂ ਕੋ ਕੌ। ੬੬੫।","roman":"Kaahe kau mo so bibaad karai su darai in te bin hee su too ko kau | 665 |","meaning_en":"why do you argue with me? You fear them for no reason.'","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਿਨ ਹੀ ਸੁ ਤੂ ਕੋ ਕੌ: read as 'for no reason'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[666],"number_text":"੬੬੬।","page":440,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨਿ ਕੈ ਜਦੁਰਾਇ ਕੀ ਬਾਤ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਬਤੀਆ ਹਰਿ ਕੇ ਇਮ ਸੰਗਿ ਉਚਾਰੀ।","roman":"Suni kai jaduraai kee baat treeyaa bateeaa hari ke im sangi uchaaree |","meaning_en":"Hearing the Yadav king's words, the woman spoke thus to Krishna:","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਾਦਨੀ ਰਾਤਿ ਰਹੀ ਛਕਿ ਕੈ ਦਿਜੀਯੈ ਹਰਿ ਹੋਵਨ ਰੈਨ ਅੰਧਯਾਰੀ।","roman":"Chaadnee raati rahee chhaki kai dijeeyai hari hovan rain andhyaaree |","meaning_en":"'The moonlit night is at its full; Krishna, let the night grow dark first;","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨ ਕੈ ਹਮਹੂੰ ਤੁਮਰੀ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਅਪਨੇ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਬਿਚਾਰੀ।","roman":"Sun kai hamhoon tumree bateeyaa apne man mai ih bhaati bichaaree |","meaning_en":"hearing your words, I have thought thus in my mind:","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਕ ਕਰੋ ਨਹੀ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਕੀ ਸੁ ਮਨੋ ਤੁਮ ਲਾਜ ਬਿਦਾ ਕਰਿ ਡਾਰੀ। ੬੬੬।","roman":"Sank karo nahee gvaarin kee su mano tum laaj bidaa kari daaree | 666 |","meaning_en":"you have no fear of the gopis; it seems you have sent shame away.","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[667],"number_text":"੬੬੭।","page":440,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਖਤ ਹੋ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਹਮ ਸੋ ਹਸਿ ਕੈ ਹਰਿ ਕੈ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਹਿਤ ਭਾਰੋ।","roman":"Bhaakhat ho bateeyaa ham so hasi kai hari kai ati hee hit bhaaro |","meaning_en":"You speak to me laughing, Krishna, with very great love;","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੁਸਕਾਤ ਹੈ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਹੇਰਿ ਉਤੈ ਪਿਖਿ ਕੈ ਹਮਰੋ ਇਹ ਕਉਤੁਕ ਸਾਰੋ।","roman":"Muskaat hai gvaarin heri utai pikhi kai hamro ih kautuk saaro |","meaning_en":"the gopis over there are smiling, seeing all this play of ours;","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਛੋਰ ਦੈ ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਹਮ ਕੋ ਅਪਨੇ ਮਨ ਬੁਧਿ ਅਕਾਮ ਕੀ ਧਾਰੋ।","roman":"Chhor dai kaanh kahiyo ham ko apne man budhi akaam kee dhaaro |","meaning_en":"let me go, Kanh,' she said, 'and keep in your mind a thought free of desire;","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਤੇ ਤੋ ਸੰਗਿ ਮੈ ਸੋ ਕਹੋ ਜਦੁਰਾਇ ਘਨੀ ਤੁਮ ਸੰਕ ਬਿਚਾਰੋ। ੬੬੭।","roman":"Taahee te to sangi mai so kaho jaduraai ghanee tum sank bichaaro | 667 |","meaning_en":"that is why I say this to you, Yadav king: consider with great care.'","page":440,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[668],"number_text":"੬੬੮।","page":441,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭੂਖ ਲਗੇ ਸੁਨੀਐ ਸਜਨੀ ਲਗਰਾ ਕਹੂੰ ਛੋਰਤ ਜਾਤ ਬਗੀ ਕੋ।","roman":"Bhookh lage suneeai sajnee lagraa kahoon chhorat jaat bagee ko |","meaning_en":"'Listen, friend: when it is hungry, does a falcon ever let go of a heron?","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Krishna's reply. ਲਗਰਾ: read as the lagar falcon; ਬਗੀ: 'heron'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਤ ਕੀ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਸੁਨੀ ਤੈ ਕਥਾ ਬਿਰਹੀ ਨਹਿ ਛੋਰਤ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਲਗੀ ਕੋ।","roman":"Taat kee syaam sunee tai kathaa birhee nahi chhorat preeti lagee ko |","meaning_en":"Have you heard the tale, dear? One in love's longing does not let go of the love he is bound to;","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਾਤ ਕੀ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਸੁਨੀ ਤੈ ਕਥਾ: read as 'have you heard the tale, dear'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਛੋਰਤ ਹੈ ਸੁ ਨਹੀ ਕੁਟਵਾਰ ਕਿਧੌ ਗਹਿ ਕੈ ਪੁਰ ਹੂੰ ਕੀ ਠਗੀ ਕੋ।","roman":"Chhorat hai su nahee kutvaar kidhau gahi kai pur hoon kee thagee ko |","meaning_en":"a city magistrate does not let go of a town's swindler once he has seized him;","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕੁਟਵਾਰ: kotwal, city police chief."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਤੇ ਨ ਛੋਰਤ ਹਉ ਤੁਮ ਕੌ ਕਿ ਸੁਨਿਯੋ ਕਹੂੰ ਛੋਰਤ ਸਿੰਘ ਮ੍ਰਿਗੀ ਕੋ। ੬੬੮।","roman":"Taa te na chhorat hau tum kau ki suniyo kahoon chhorat singh mrigee ko | 668 |","meaning_en":"so I will not let you go; have you ever heard of a lion letting go of a doe?'","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[669],"number_text":"੬੬੯।","page":441,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੀ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਇਹ ਬਾਲ ਕੇ ਸੰਗ ਜੁ ਥੀ ਅਤਿ ਜੋਬਨ ਕੇ ਰਸ ਭੀਨੀ।","roman":"Kahee bateeyaa ih baal ke sang ju thee ati joban ke ras bheenee |","meaning_en":"He said these words to the young woman, who was steeped in the delight of youth,","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚੰਦ੍ਰਭਗਾ ਅਰੁ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਤੇ ਅਤਿ ਰੂਪ ਕੇ ਬੀਚ ਹੁਤੀ ਜੁ ਨਵੀਨੀ।","roman":"Chandrabhgaa aru gvaarin te ati roop ke beech hutee ju naveenee |","meaning_en":"and who was fresher in beauty than Chandrabhaga and the other gopis;","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਉ ਮ੍ਰਿਗਰਾਜ ਮ੍ਰਿਗੀ ਕੋ ਗਹੈ ਕਬਿ ਨੈ ਉਪਮਾ ਬਿਧਿ ਯਾ ਲਖਿ ਲੀਨੀ।","roman":"Jiu mrigraaj mrigee ko gahai kabi nai upmaa bidhi yaa lakhi leenee |","meaning_en":"as the king of beasts seizes a doe — so the poet perceived the likeness —","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਤਬੈ ਕਰਵਾ ਗਹ ਕੈ ਅਪਨੇ ਬਲ ਸੰਗਿ ਸੋਊ ਬਸਿ ਕੀਨੀ। ੬੬੯।","roman":"Kaanh tabai karvaa gah kai apne bal sangi so'oo basi keenee | 669 |","meaning_en":"Kanh then, seizing her by the hand, brought her under his power by his strength.","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[670],"number_text":"੬੭੦।","page":441,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰਿ ਕੈ ਬਸਿ ਵਾ ਸੰਗਿ ਐਸੇ ਕਹੀ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਜਦੁਰਾਇ ਕਹਾਨੀ।","roman":"Kari kai basi vaa sangi aise kahee kabi syaam kahai jaduraai kahaanee |","meaning_en":"Having won her over, the Yadav king told her a tale thus, says the poet Shyam,","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੈ ਰਸ ਰੀਤਹਿ ਕੀ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਜੁ ਹੁਤੀ ਸਮ ਮਾਨਹੁ ਅੰਮ੍ਰਿਤ ਬਾਨੀ।","roman":"Pai ras reethi kee ati hee ju hutee sam maanhu anmrit baanee |","meaning_en":"full of the ways of love, like nectar speech:","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੇਰੋ ਕਹਾ ਬਿਗਰੈ ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਨਾਰਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਗੁਮਾਨੀ।","roman":"Tero kahaa bigrai brij naari kahiyo ih bhaati syaam gumaanee |","meaning_en":"'What harm comes to you, woman of Braj?' So spoke proud Shyam;","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਸਭੈ ਤ੍ਰੀਯ ਚੇਰਿਨ ਹੈ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਤਿਨ ਮੈ ਤੂ ਰਾਨੀ। ੬੭੦।","roman":"Aur sabhai treey cherin hai brikhbhaan sutaa tin mai too raanee | 670 |","meaning_en":"'all the other women are maidservants; among them, daughter of Brikhbhan, you are the queen.'","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[671],"number_text":"੬੭੧।","page":441,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹਾ ਚੰਦ ਕੀ ਚਾਦਨੀ ਛਾਜਤ ਹੈ ਜਹਾ ਪਾਤ ਚੰਬੇਲੀ ਕੇ ਸੇਜ ਡਹੀ ਹੈ।","roman":"Jahaa chand kee chaadnee chhaajat hai jahaa paat chanbelee ke sej dahee hai |","meaning_en":"Where the moonlight spreads, where a bed of jasmine leaves is laid,","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੇਤ ਜਹਾ ਗੁਲ ਰਾਜਤ ਹੈ ਜਿਹ ਕੇ ਜਮੁਨਾ ਢਿਗ ਆਇ ਬਹੀ ਹੈ।","roman":"Set jahaa gul raajat hai jih ke jamunaa dhig aai bahee hai |","meaning_en":"where white flowers shine, and near which the Yamuna comes flowing —","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਸਮੈ ਹਰਿ ਰਾਧੇ ਗ੍ਰਸੀ ਉਪਮਾ ਤਿਹ ਕੀ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੀ ਹੈ।","roman":"Taahee samai hari raadhe grasee upmaa tih kee kabi syaam kahee hai |","meaning_en":"at that time Krishna embraced Radha; the poet Shyam told its likeness:","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੇਤ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਤਨ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਹਰੀ ਮਨੋ ਸੋਮ ਕਲਾ ਇਹ ਰਾਹੁ ਗਹੀ ਹੈ। ੬੭੧।","roman":"Set treeyaa tan syaam haree mano som kalaa ih raahu gahee hai | 671 |","meaning_en":"the woman's body fair, Krishna's dark, as if Rahu had seized a digit of the moon.","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[672],"number_text":"੬੭੨।","page":441,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਹ ਕੋ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਫਿਰਿ ਛੋਰਿ ਦਯੋ ਸੋਊ ਕੁੰਜ ਗਲੀ ਕੇ ਬਿਖੈ ਬਨ ਮੈ।","roman":"Tih ko hari joo phiri chhori dayo so'oo kunj galee ke bikhai ban mai |","meaning_en":"Then Krishna let her go, there in the arbour lane in the forest;","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਫਿਰਿ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਮੈ ਸੋਊ ਜਾਇ ਮਿਲੀ ਅਤਿ ਆਨੰਦ ਕੈ ਅਪੁਨੇ ਤਨ ਮੈ।","roman":"Phiri gvaarin mai so'oo jaai milee ati aanand kai apune tan mai |","meaning_en":"then she went and joined the gopis, with great joy in her body;","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਤਾ ਛਬਿ ਕੀ ਉਪਮਾ ਹੈ ਕਹੀ ਉਪਜੀ ਜੁ ਕੋਊ ਕਬਿ ਕੈ ਮਨ ਮੈ।","roman":"Ati taa chhabi kee upmaa hai kahee upjee ju ko'oo kabi kai man mai |","meaning_en":"the likeness of that sight, as it arose in the poet's mind, is told:","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਨੋ ਕੇਹਰਿ ਤੇ ਛੁਟਵਾਇ ਮਿਲੀ ਮ੍ਰਿਗਨੀ ਕੋ ਮਨੋ ਮ੍ਰਿਗੀਯਾ ਬਨ ਮੈ। ੬੭੨।","roman":"Mano kehri te chhutvaai milee mrignee ko mano mrigeeyaa ban mai | 672 |","meaning_en":"as if a doe, freed from a lion, had joined the does in the forest.","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[673],"number_text":"੬੭੩।","page":441,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਫਿਰਿ ਜਾਇ ਕੈ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਮੈ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਇਕ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਖੇਲ ਮਚਾਯੋ।","roman":"Phiri jaai kai gvaarin mai hari joo ati hee ik sundar khel machaayo |","meaning_en":"Then, going among the gopis, Krishna started a very beautiful play;","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚੰਦ੍ਰਭਗਾ ਹੂੰ ਕੇ ਹਾਥ ਪੈ ਹਾਥ ਧਰਿਯੋ ਅਤਿ ਸਹੀ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਸੁਖੁ ਪਾਯੋ।","roman":"Chandrabhgaa hoon ke haath pai haath dhariyo ati sahee man mai sukhu paayo |","meaning_en":"he put his hand on Chandrabhaga's hand and felt great joy in his heart;","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਾਵਤ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਹੈ ਸਭ ਗੀਤ ਜੋਊ ਉਨ ਕੈ ਮਨ ਭੀਤਰ ਭਾਯੋ।","roman":"Gaavat gvaarin hai sabh geet jo'oo un kai man bheetar bhaayo |","meaning_en":"the gopis all sing whatever songs please their hearts;","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਮਨਿ ਆਨੰਦ ਕੈ ਮਨ ਕੋ ਫੁਨਿ ਸੋਕ ਸਭੈ ਬਿਸਰਾਯੋ। ੬੭੩।","roman":"Syaam kahai mani aanand kai man ko phuni sok sabhai bisraayo | 673 |","meaning_en":"Shyam says, with joy in their minds, they forgot all sorrow of heart.","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[674],"number_text":"੬੭੪।","page":441,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਰਿ ਨਾਚਤ ਨਾਚਤ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਮੈ ਹਸਿ ਚੰਦ੍ਰਭਗਾ ਹੂੰ ਕੀ ਓਰਿ ਨਿਹਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Hari naachat naachat gvaarin mai hasi chandrabhgaa hoon kee ori nihaariyo |","meaning_en":"Dancing and dancing among the gopis, Krishna smiled and looked towards Chandrabhaga;","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋਊ ਹਸੀ ਇਤ ਤੇ ਏ ਹਸੇ ਜਦੁਰਾ ਤਿਹ ਸੋ ਬਚਨਾ ਹੈ ਉਚਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"So'oo hasee it te e hase jaduraa tih so bachnaa hai uchaariyo |","meaning_en":"she smiled, and from this side he smiled; the Yadav king spoke words to her:","page":441,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੇਰੋ ਮਹਾ ਹਿਤ ਹੈ ਤੁਮ ਸੋ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਇਹ ਹੇਰਿ ਬਿਚਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Mero mahaa hit hai tum so brikhbhaan sutaa ih heri bichaariyo |","meaning_en":"'I have great love for you.' Brikhbhan's daughter saw this and thought:","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਨਿ ਤ੍ਰਿਯਾ ਸੰਗਿ ਹੇਤ ਕਰਿਯੋ ਹਮ ਊਪਰ ਤੇ ਹਰਿ ਚੇਤ ਬਿਸਾਰਿਯੋ। ੬੭੪।","roman":"Aani triyaa sangi het kariyo ham oopar te hari chet bisaariyo | 674 |","meaning_en":"'Krishna has given his love to another woman and put me out of his mind.'","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[675],"number_text":"੬੭੫।","page":442,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਰਿ ਰਾਧਿਕਾ ਆਨਨ ਦੇਖਤ ਹੀ ਅਪਨੇ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਉਚਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Hari raadhikaa aanan dekhat hee apne man mai ih bhaati uchaariyo |","meaning_en":"Looking at Krishna's face, Radhika said thus within her mind;","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਭਏ ਬਸਿ ਅਉਰ ਤ੍ਰਿਯਾ ਤਿਹ ਤੇ ਅਤਿ ਪੈ ਮਨਿ ਮਾਨ ਹੀ ਧਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Syaam bhae basi aur triyaa tih te ati pai mani maan hee dhaariyo |","meaning_en":"Shyam had come under the sway of another woman; so she took deep offence in her heart;","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਾਨ: wounded pride, a lover's sulk."},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਨੰਦ ਥੋ ਜਿਤਨੋ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਤਿਤਨੋ ਇਹ ਭਾਖਿ ਬਿਦਾ ਕਰਿ ਡਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Aanand tho jitno man mai titno ih bhaakhi bidaa kari daariyo |","meaning_en":"all the joy there was in her heart, she sent it all away, saying this:","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚੰਦ੍ਰਭਗਾ ਮੁਖਿ ਚੰਦ ਦੁਤੈ ਸਭ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਤੇ ਘਟ ਮੋਹਿ ਬਿਚਾਰਿਯੋ। ੬੭੫।","roman":"Chandrabhgaa mukhi chand dutai sabh gvaarin te ghat mohi bichaariyo | 675 |","meaning_en":"'He thinks Chandrabhaga's face has the moon's splendour, and counts me less than all the gopis.'","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[676],"number_text":"੬੭੬।","page":442,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹਿ ਕੈ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਸੋਊ ਤਬ ਹੀ ਅਪਨੇ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਇਹ ਬਾਤ ਬਿਚਾਰੀ।","roman":"Kahi kai ih bhaati so'oo tab hee apne man mai ih baat bichaaree |","meaning_en":"Having said this, she then considered this matter in her mind:","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰੀਤ ਕਰੀ ਹਰਿ ਆਨਹਿ ਸੋ ਤਜਿ ਖੇਲ ਸਭੈ ਉਠਿ ਧਾਮਿ ਸਿਧਾਰੀ।","roman":"Preet karee hari aanhi so taji khel sabhai uthi dhaami sidhaaree |","meaning_en":"'Krishna has loved another'; leaving all the play, she rose and went home;","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਐਸ ਕਰੀ ਗਨਤੀ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਉਪਮਾ ਤਿਹ ਕੀ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਉਚਾਰੀ।","roman":"Ais karee gantee man mai upmaa tih kee kabi syaam uchaaree |","meaning_en":"she reckoned thus in her mind; the poet Shyam told its likeness:","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਰੀਯਨ ਬੀਚ ਚਲੈਗੀ ਕਥਾ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨੁ ਸੁਤਾ ਬ੍ਰਿਜਨਾਥਿ ਬਿਸਾਰੀ। ੬੭੬।","roman":"Treeyan beech chalaigee kathaa brikhbhaanu sutaa brijnaathi bisaaree | 676 |","meaning_en":"'The story will go round among the women that the lord of Braj forgot Brikhbhan's daughter.'","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"section_heading","name":"ਅਥ ਰਾਧਿਕਾ ਕੋ ਮਾਨ ਕਥਨੰ","gurmukhi":"ਅਥ ਰਾਧਿਕਾ ਕੋ ਮਾਨ ਕਥਨੰ","roman":"Ath raadhikaa ko maan kathnan","meaning_en":"Now is told Radhika's pique.","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਾਨ: a lover's sulking or wounded pride."},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[677],"number_text":"੬੭੭।","page":442,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਚਲੀ ਕਹਿ ਕੈ ਸੁ ਤ੍ਰਿਯਾ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਸੋਊ ਕੁੰਜ ਗਲੀ ਹੈ।","roman":"Ih bhaati chalee kahi kai su triyaa kabi syaam kahai so'oo kunj galee hai |","meaning_en":"Saying this, the woman went away, says the poet Shyam, into the arbour lane;","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚੰਦਮੁਖੀ ਤਨ ਕੰਚਨ ਸੇ ਸਭ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਤੇ ਜੋਊ ਖੂਬ ਭਲੀ ਹੈ।","roman":"Chandmukhee tan kanchan se sabh gvaarin te jo'oo khoob bhalee hai |","meaning_en":"moon-faced, golden-bodied, she who is the finest of all the gopis;","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਨ ਕੀਯੋ ਨਿਖਰੀ ਤਿਨ ਤੇ ਮ੍ਰਿਗਨੀ ਸੀ ਮਨੋ ਸੁ ਬਿਨਾ ਹੀ ਅਲੀ ਹੈ।","roman":"Maan keeyo nikhree tin te mrignee see mano su binaa hee alee hai |","meaning_en":"in pique she broke away from them, like a doe, quite without a companion;","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਿਖਰੀ: 'separated'; ਅਲੀ: 'companion'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਉਪਜੀ ਉਪਮਾ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਪਤਿ ਸੋ ਰਤਿ ਮਾਨਹੁ ਰੂਠਿ ਚਲੀ ਹੈ। ੬੭੭।","roman":"Yau upjee upmaa man mai pati so rati maanhu roothi chalee hai | 677 |","meaning_en":"this likeness arose in the mind: as if Rati had gone off sulking from her husband.","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[678],"number_text":"੬੭੮।","page":442,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਤ ਤੇ ਹਰਿ ਖੇਲਤ ਰਾਸ ਬਿਖੈ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਕਰਿ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਨਿਹਾਰੀ।","roman":"It te hari khelat raas bikhai brikhbhaan sutaa kari preeti nihaaree |","meaning_en":"Here Krishna, playing in the Ras, looked with love for Brikhbhan's daughter;","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Ras: the circle dance."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੇਖ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਨ ਪਿਖੀ ਤਿਨ ਮੈ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਜੁ ਹੁਤੀ ਸੋਊ ਪਿਆਰੀ।","roman":"Pekh rahiyo na pikhee tin mai kabi syaam kahai ju hutee so'oo piaaree |","meaning_en":"he kept looking but did not see among them, says the poet Shyam, the one who was his beloved,","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚੰਦ੍ਰਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਸਮ ਜਾ ਮੁਖ ਹੈ ਤਨ ਕੰਚਨ ਸੋ ਅਤਿ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਨਾਰੀ।","roman":"Chandraprabhaa sam jaa mukh hai tan kanchan so ati sundar naaree |","meaning_en":"the very beautiful woman whose face is like moonlight and whose body is like gold.","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੈ ਗ੍ਰਿਹਿ ਮਾਨ ਕੈ ਨੀਦ ਗਈ ਕਿ ਕੋਊ ਉਨਿ ਮਾਨ ਕੀ ਬਾਤ ਬਿਚਾਰੀ। ੬੭੮।","roman":"Kai grihi maan kai need gaee ki ko'oo uni maan kee baat bichaaree | 678 |","meaning_en":"'Has she gone home in pique and fallen asleep, or has she taken some offence?'","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Kaanh baach","meaning_en":"Kanh said:","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[679],"number_text":"੬੭੯।","page":442,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਜਛਟਾ ਜਿਹ ਨਾਮ ਸਖੀ ਕੋ ਹੈ ਸੋਊ ਸਖੀ ਜਦੁਰਾਇ ਬੁਲਾਈ।","roman":"Bijachhtaa jih naam sakhee ko hai so'oo sakhee jaduraai bulaaee |","meaning_en":"The friend named Bijchhata — that friend the Yadav king called;","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Name ਬਿਜਛਟਾ transliterated Bijchhata."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਜਿਹ ਕੰਚਨ ਸੀ ਜਿਹ ਤੇ ਮੁਖ ਚੰਦ ਛਟਾ ਛਬਿ ਪਾਈ।","roman":"Ang prabhaa jih kanchan see jih te mukh chand chhataa chhabi paaee |","meaning_en":"her limbs glowed like gold, and from her the moon's face took its splendour;","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਸੰਗਿ ਐਸੇ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਹਰਿਜੂ ਸੁਨ ਤੂ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਪਹਿ ਜਾਈ।","roman":"Taa sangi aise kahiyo harijoo sun too brikhbhaan sutaa pahi jaaee |","meaning_en":"Krishna said to her thus: 'Listen, go to Brikhbhan's daughter;","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਇਨ ਪੈ ਬਿਨਤੀਅਨ ਕੈ ਅਤਿ ਹੇਤ ਕੇ ਭਾਵ ਸੋ ਲਿਆਉ ਮਨਾਈ। ੬੭੯।","roman":"Paain pai binteean kai ati het ke bhaav so liaau manaaee | 679 |","meaning_en":"fall at her feet, make entreaties, and with feelings of deep love bring her round.'","page":442,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[680],"number_text":"੬੮੦।","page":443,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਦੁਰਾਇ ਕੀ ਸੁਨ ਕੈ ਬਤੀਆ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਜੋਊ ਬਾਲ ਭਲੀ ਹੈ।","roman":"Jaduraai kee sun kai bateeaa brikhbhaan sutaa jo'oo baal bhalee hai |","meaning_en":"Hearing the Yadav king's words about Brikhbhan's daughter, who is a fine young woman,","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੂਪ ਮਨੋ ਸਮ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਮੈਨ ਕੇ ਮਾਨਹੁ ਸੁੰਦਰਿ ਕੰਜ ਕਲੀ ਹੈ।","roman":"Roop mano sam sundar main ke maanhu sundri kanj kalee hai |","meaning_en":"whose beauty is like Kamdev's own, as if she were a lovely lotus bud,","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਕੇ ਮਨਾਇਬੇ ਕਾਜ ਚਲੀ ਹਰਿ ਕੋ ਫੁਨਿ ਆਇਸ ਪਾਇ ਅਲੀ ਹੈ।","roman":"Taa ke manaaibe kaaj chalee hari ko phuni aais paai alee hai |","meaning_en":"the friend, receiving Krishna's command, set off to win her over;","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੋ ਉਪਜੀ ਜੀਯ ਮੈ ਉਪਮਾ ਕਰ ਤੇ ਚਕਈ ਮਨੋ ਛੂਟਿ ਚਲੀ ਹੈ। ੬੮੦।","roman":"Yo upjee jeey mai upmaa kar te chakaee mano chhooti chalee hai | 680 |","meaning_en":"this likeness arose in the mind: as if a chakvi bird had slipped from the hand and flown off.","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚਕਈ: the female chakva (ruddy shelduck)."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਸਖੀ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਸਖੀ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Sakhee baach","meaning_en":"The friend said:","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[681],"number_text":"੬੮੧।","page":443,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਜ ਛਟਾ ਜਿਹ ਨਾਮ ਸਖੀ ਕੋ ਸੋਊ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਪਹਿ ਆਈ।","roman":"Bij chhataa jih naam sakhee ko so'oo brikhbhaan sutaa pahi aaee |","meaning_en":"The friend named Bijchhata came to Brikhbhan's daughter;","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਇ ਕੈ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਐਸੇ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਸੁਨ ਤੂ ਰੀ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਬ੍ਰਿਜਨਾਥਿ ਬੁਲਾਈ।","roman":"Aai kai sundar aise kahiyo sun too ree treeyaa brijnaathi bulaaee |","meaning_en":"coming, the fair one said thus: 'Listen, woman, the lord of Braj has called you.'","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੋ ਬ੍ਰਿਜਨਾਥ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਨਾਰਿ ਸੁ ਕੋ ਕਨ੍ਹਈਯਾ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਕਉਨ ਕਨਾਈ।","roman":"Ko brijnaath kahiyo brij naari su ko kanhaeeyaa kahiyo kaun kanaaee |","meaning_en":"'Who is the lord of Braj?' said the woman of Braj; 'who is Kanhaiya? Who is Kanhai?","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Radha's reply begins mid-verse."},{"gurmukhi":"ਖੇਲਹੁ ਤਾ ਹੀ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਸੰਗਿ ਲਾਲ ਰੀ ਕੋ ਜਿਹ ਕੇ ਸੰਗਿ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਲਗਾਈ। ੬੮੧।","roman":"Khelhu taa hee treeyaa sangi laal ree ko jih ke sangi preeti lagaaee | 681 |","meaning_en":"Let the darling play with that very woman with whom he has fallen in love.'","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[682],"number_text":"੬੮੨।","page":443,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਜਨੀ ਨੰਦ ਲਾਲ ਬੁਲਾਵਤ ਹੈ ਅਪਨੇ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਹਠ ਰੰਚ ਨ ਕੀਜੈ।","roman":"Sajnee nand laal bulaavat hai apne man mai hath ranch na keejai |","meaning_en":"'Friend, Nand's darling is calling you; do not be the least bit stubborn in your heart;","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਈ ਹੋ ਹਉ ਚਲਿ ਕੈ ਤੁਮ ਪੈ ਤਿਹ ਤੇ ਸੁ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਅਬ ਮਾਨ ਹੀ ਲੀਜੈ।","roman":"Aaee ho hau chali kai tum pai tih te su kahiyo ab maan hee leejai |","meaning_en":"I have come to you on his account; so do as he says now, and accept;","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਾਨ ਹੀ ਲੀਜੈ: 'accept, agree' (play on ਮਾਨ, pique)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੇਗ ਚਲੋ ਜਦੁਰਾਇ ਕੇ ਪਾਸ ਕਛੂ ਤੁਮਰੋ ਇਹ ਤੇ ਨਹੀ ਛੀਜੈ।","roman":"Beg chalo jaduraai ke paas kachhoo tumro ih te nahee chheejai |","meaning_en":"go quickly to the Yadav king; you lose nothing by this;","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਤੇ ਬਾਤ ਕਹੋ ਤੁਮ ਸੋ ਸੁਖ ਆਪਨ ਲੈ ਸੁਖ ਅਉਰਨ ਦੀਜੈ। ੬੮੨।","roman":"Taahee te baat kaho tum so sukh aapan lai sukh auran deejai | 682 |","meaning_en":"that is why I tell you this: take joy yourself and give joy to others.'","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[683],"number_text":"੬੮੩।","page":443,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਤੇ ਕਰੋ ਨਹੀ ਮਾਨ ਸਖੀ ਉਠਿ ਬੇਗ ਚਲੋ ਸਿਖ ਮਾਨਿ ਹਮਾਰੀ।","roman":"Taa te karo nahee maan sakhee uthi beg chalo sikh maani hamaaree |","meaning_en":"'So do not sulk, friend; rise and go quickly, take my advice;","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੁਰਲੀ ਜਹ ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਬਜਾਵਤ ਹੈ ਬਹਸੈ ਤਹ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਗਾਰੀ।","roman":"Murlee jah kaanh bajaavat hai bahsai tah gvaarin sundar gaaree |","meaning_en":"where Kanh plays the flute, the gopis there exchange pretty teasing songs;","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਹਸੈ ... ਗਾਰੀ: read as 'banter in teasing songs (gaari)'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਤੇ ਤੋ ਸੋ ਕਹੋ ਚਲੀਐ ਕਛੁ ਸੰਕ ਕਰੋ ਨ ਮਨੈ ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਨਾਰੀ।","roman":"Taahee te to so kaho chaleeai kachhu sank karo na manai brij naaree |","meaning_en":"so I tell you, let us go; have no doubt in your mind, woman of Braj;","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਇਨ ਤੋਰੇ ਪਰੋ ਤਜਿ ਸੰਕ ਨਿਸੰਕ ਚਲੋ ਹਰਿ ਪਾਸਿਹ ਹਹਾ ਰੀ। ੬੮੩।","roman":"Paain tore paro taji sank nisank chalo hari paasih hahaa ree | 683 |","meaning_en":"I fall at your feet; leave your doubts and go to Krishna without fear, I beg you.'","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹਹਾ: an exclamation of entreaty."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[684],"number_text":"੬੮੪।","page":443,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਕ ਕਛੂ ਨ ਕਰੋ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਤਜਿ ਸੰਕ ਨਿਸੰਕ ਚਲੋ ਸੁਨਿ ਮਾਨਨਿ।","roman":"Sank kachhoo na karo man mai taji sank nisank chalo suni maanni |","meaning_en":"'Have no doubt at all in your mind; leave doubt and go without fear, listen, proud one;","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੇਰੇ ਮੈ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਮਹਾ ਹਰਿ ਕੀ ਤਿਹ ਤੇ ਹਉ ਕਹੋ ਤੁਹਿ ਸੰਗ ਗੁਮਾਨਨਿ।","roman":"Tere mai preeti mahaa hari kee tih te hau kaho tuhi sang gumaanni |","meaning_en":"Krishna has great love for you; that is why I tell you this, haughty one;","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨੈਨ ਬਨੇ ਤੁਮਰੇ ਸਰ ਸੇ ਸੁ ਧਰੇ ਮਨੋ ਤੀਛਨ ਮੈਨ ਕੀ ਸਾਨਨਿ।","roman":"Nain bane tumre sar se su dhare mano teechhan main kee saanni |","meaning_en":"your eyes are made like arrows, as if sharpened on Kamdev's whetstone;","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੋ ਹੀ ਸੋ ਪ੍ਰੇਮ ਮਹਾ ਹਰਿ ਕੋ ਇਹ ਬਾਤ ਹੀ ਤੇ ਕਛੂ ਹਉ ਹੂੰ ਅਜਾਨਨਿ। ੬੮੪।","roman":"To hee so prem mahaa hari ko ih baat hee te kachhoo hau hoon ajaanni | 684 |","meaning_en":"Krishna's great love is for you alone; I know nothing beyond this.'","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Last clause read loosely; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[685],"number_text":"੬੮੫।","page":443,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੁਰਲੀ ਜਦੁਬੀਰ ਬਜਾਵਤ ਹੈ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਅਤਿ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਠਉਰੈ।","roman":"Murlee jadubeer bajaavat hai kabi syaam kahai ati sundar thaurai |","meaning_en":"'The Yadav hero is playing the flute, says the poet Shyam, in a very beautiful place;","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਤੇ ਤੇਰੇ ਪਾਸਿ ਪਠੀ ਸੁ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਤਿਹ ਲਿਆਵ ਸੁ ਜਾਇ ਕੈ ਦਉਰੈ।","roman":"Taahee te tere paasi pathee su kahiyo tih liaav su jaai kai daurai |","meaning_en":"that is why he sent me to you, saying, \"Run and bring her\";","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਾਚਤ ਹੈ ਜਹ ਚੰਦ੍ਰਭਗਾ ਅਰੁ ਗਾਇ ਕੈ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਲੇਤ ਹੈ ਭਉਰੈ।","roman":"Naachat hai jah chandrabhgaa aru gaai kai gvaarni let hai bhaurai |","meaning_en":"there Chandrabhaga dances, and the gopis sing and whirl in circles;","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਉਰੈ: read as 'whirling rounds'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਤੇ ਬੇਗ ਚਲੋ ਸਜਨੀ ਤੁਮਰੇ ਬਿਨ ਹੀ ਰਸ ਲੂਟਤ ਅਉਰੈ। ੬੮੫।","roman":"Taahee te beg chalo sajnee tumre bin hee ras lootat aurai | 685 |","meaning_en":"so come quickly, friend; without you, others are carrying off the delight.'","page":443,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[686],"number_text":"੬੮੬।","page":444,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਤੇ ਬਾਲ ਬਲਾਇ ਲਿਉ ਤੇਰੀ ਮੈ ਬੇਗ ਚਲੋ ਨੰਦ ਲਾਲ ਬੁਲਾਵੈ।","roman":"Taahee te baal balaai liu teree mai beg chalo nand laal bulaavai |","meaning_en":"'So, girl, may I take your troubles on myself; come quickly, Nand's darling is calling;","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਲਾਇ ਲਿਉ: an expression of affection, 'may your ills fall on me'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਬਜਾਵਤ ਹੈ ਮੁਰਲੀ ਜਹ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨੀਯਾ ਮਿਲਿ ਮੰਗਲ ਗਾਵੈ।","roman":"Syaam bajaavat hai murlee jah gvaarineeyaa mili mangal gaavai |","meaning_en":"where Shyam plays the flute, the gopis together sing songs of joy;","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋਰਠਿ ਸੁਧ ਮਲਾਰ ਬਿਲਾਵਲ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਨੰਦ ਲਾਲ ਰਿਝਾਵੈ।","roman":"Sorthi sudh malaar bilaaval syaam kahai nand laal rijhaavai |","meaning_en":"in Sorath, pure Malar and Bilawal, says Shyam, they delight Nand's darling;","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਕੀ ਬਾਤ ਕਹਾ ਕਹੀਯੇ ਸੁਰ ਤ੍ਯਾਗਿ ਸਭੈ ਸੁਰ ਮੰਡਲ ਆਵੈ। ੬੮੬।","roman":"Aur kee baat kahaa kaheeye sur tyaagi sabhai sur mandal aavai | 686 |","meaning_en":"what to say of others? The gods, leaving everything, come from the heavenly realm.'","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ ਪ੍ਰਤਿ ਉਤਰ","gurmukhi":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ ਪ੍ਰਤਿ ਉਤਰ","roman":"Raadhe baach prati utar","meaning_en":"Radha said in reply:","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[687],"number_text":"੬੮੭।","page":444,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੈ ਨ ਚਲੋ ਸਜਨੀ ਹਰਿ ਪੈ ਜੁ ਚਲੋ ਤਬ ਮੋਹਿ ਬ੍ਰਿਜਨਾਥ ਦੁਹਾਈ।","roman":"Mai na chalo sajnee hari pai ju chalo tab mohi brijnaath duhaaee |","meaning_en":"'I will not go to Krishna, friend; if I go, I swear by the lord of Braj;","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦੁਹਾਈ: an oath or curse; read as 'I swear'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੋ ਸੰਗ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਤਜੀ ਜਦੁਨੰਦਨ ਚੰਦ੍ਰਭਗਾ ਸੰਗਿ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਲਗਾਈ।","roman":"Mo sang preeti tajee jadunandan chandrabhgaa sangi preeti lagaaee |","meaning_en":"the son of the Yadavs has given up his love for me and has fallen in love with Chandrabhaga.'","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕੀ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਮਹਾ ਤੁਮ ਸੌ ਤਜਿ ਮਾਨ ਹਹਾ ਰੀ ਚਲੋ ਦੁਚਿਤਾਈ।","roman":"Syaam kee preeti mahaa tum sau taji maan hahaa ree chalo duchitaaee |","meaning_en":"'Shyam's love for you is great; leave your pique, I beg you, and come, putting away your doubts;","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"The messenger speaks."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੇਰੇ ਬਿਨਾ ਨਹੀ ਖੇਲਤ ਹੈ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਖੇਲਹੁ ਜਾਹੂੰ ਸੋ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਲਗਾਈ। ੬੮੭।","roman":"Tere binaa nahee khelat hai kahiyo khelhu jaahoon so preeti lagaaee | 687 |","meaning_en":"he will not play without you.' She said: 'Let him play with the one he has fallen in love with.'","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਦੂਤੀ ਵਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਦੂਤੀ ਵਾਚ","roman":"Dootee vaach","meaning_en":"The messenger said:","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦੂਤੀ: female go-between."},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[688],"number_text":"੬੮੮।","page":444,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਇ ਪਰੋ ਤੁਮਰੇ ਸਜਨੀ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਮਨ ਭੀਤਰ ਮਾਨੁ ਨ ਕਈਯੈ।","roman":"Paai paro tumre sajnee ati hee man bheetar maanu na kaeeyai |","meaning_en":"'I fall at your feet, friend; do not hold such pique in your heart;","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਬੁਲਾਵਤ ਹੈ ਸੁ ਜਹਾ ਉਠ ਕੈ ਤਿਹ ਠਉਰ ਬਿਖੈ ਚਲਿ ਜਈਯੈ।","roman":"Syaam bulaavat hai su jahaa uth kai tih thaur bikhai chali jaeeyai |","meaning_en":"rise and go to the place where Shyam is calling you;","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਾਚਤ ਹੈ ਜਿਮ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿਆ ਨਚੀਯੈ ਤਿਮ ਅਉ ਤਿਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਹੀ ਗਈਯੈ।","roman":"Naachat hai jim gvaarniaa nacheeyai tim au tih bhaati hee gaeeyai |","meaning_en":"as the gopis are dancing, so dance, and sing in the same way;","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਅਨੇਕਿਕ ਬਾਤ ਕਰੋ ਪਰ ਰਾਧੇ ਬਲਾਇ ਲਿਉ ਸਉਹ ਨ ਖਈਯੈ। ੬੮੮।","roman":"Aur anekik baat karo par raadhe balaai liu sauh na khaeeyai | 688 |","meaning_en":"say a great many other things, but, Radha, may I take your troubles on me, do not swear an oath.'","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Raadhe baach","meaning_en":"Radha said:","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[689],"number_text":"੬੮੯।","page":444,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੈਹਉ ਨ ਹਉ ਸੁਨ ਰੀ ਸਜਨੀ ਤੁਹਿ ਸੀ ਹਰਿ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਕੋਟਿ ਪਠਾਵੈ।","roman":"Jaihau na hau sun ree sajnee tuhi see hari gvaarni koti pathaavai |","meaning_en":"'I will not go, listen, friend, even if Krishna sends ten million gopis like you;","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੰਸੀ ਬਜਾਵੈ ਤਹਾ ਤੁ ਕਹਾ ਅਰੁ ਆਪ ਕਹਾ ਭਯੋ ਮੰਗਲ ਗਾਵੈ।","roman":"Bansee bajaavai tahaa tu kahaa aru aap kahaa bhayo mangal gaavai |","meaning_en":"what is it to you if he plays the flute there, and what is it if he himself sings songs of joy?","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੈ ਨ ਚਲੋ ਤਿਹ ਠਉਰ ਬਿਖੈ ਬ੍ਰਹਮਾ ਹਮ ਕੋ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਆਨਿ ਸੁਨਾਵੈ।","roman":"Mai na chalo tih thaur bikhai brahmaa ham ko kahiyo aani sunaavai |","meaning_en":"I will not go to that place even if Brahma came and told me so;","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਸਖੀ ਕੀ ਕਹਾ ਗਨਤੀ ਨਹੀ ਜਾਉ ਰੀ ਜਉ ਹਰਿ ਆਪਨ ਆਵੈ। ੬੮੯।","roman":"Aur sakhee kee kahaa gantee nahee jaau ree jau hari aapan aavai | 689 |","meaning_en":"what count is there of any other friend? I will not go, even if Krishna himself comes.'","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਦੂਤੀ ਬਾਚ ਰਾਧੇ ਸੋ","gurmukhi":"ਦੂਤੀ ਬਾਚ ਰਾਧੇ ਸੋ","roman":"Dootee baach raadhe so","meaning_en":"The messenger said to Radha:","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[690],"number_text":"੬੯੦।","page":444,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਹੇ ਕੋ ਮਾਨ ਕਰੈ ਸੁਨ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਉਠ ਕੈ ਕਰ ਸੋਊ।","roman":"Kaahe ko maan karai sun gvaarin syaam kahai uth kai kar so'oo |","meaning_en":"'Why do you sulk? Listen, gopi: whatever Shyam says, rise and do that;","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾ ਕੇ ਕੀਏ ਹਰਿ ਹੋਇ ਖੁਸੀ ਸੁਨਿਯੈ ਬਲ ਕਾਜ ਕਰੋ ਅਬ ਜੋਊ।","roman":"Jaa ke kee'e hari hoi khusee suniyai bal kaaj karo ab jo'oo |","meaning_en":"listen, dear: do now whatever deed will make Krishna glad;","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਲ: read as a term of address; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਉ ਤੁਹਿ ਬੋਲਿ ਪਠਾਵਤ ਹੈ ਜਬ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਲਗੀ ਤੁਮ ਸੋ ਤਬ ਓਊ।","roman":"Tau tuhi boli pathaavat hai jab preeti lagee tum so tab o'oo |","meaning_en":"he sends for you only because he has given his love to you;","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਾਤਰ ਰਾਸ ਬਿਖੈ ਸੁਨ ਰੀ ਤੁਹਿ ਸੀ ਨਹਿ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਕੋਊ। ੬੯੦।","roman":"Naatar raas bikhai sun ree tuhi see nahi gvaarin sundar ko'oo | 690 |","meaning_en":"otherwise, listen, in the Ras there is no gopi as beautiful as you.'","page":444,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Line read loosely; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[691],"number_text":"੬੯੧।","page":445,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਗ ਤੇਰੇ ਹੀ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਘਨੀ ਹਰਿ ਕੀ ਸਭ ਜਾਨਤ ਹੈ ਕਛੂ ਨਾਹਿ ਨਈ।","roman":"Sang tere hee preeti ghanee hari kee sabh jaanat hai kachhoo naahi naee |","meaning_en":"'Krishna's deep love is with you alone; everyone knows it; it is nothing new;","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਹ ਕੀ ਮੁਖ ਉਪਮ ਚੰਦ੍ਰਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਜਿਹ ਕੀ ਤਨ ਭਾ ਮਨੋ ਰੂਪ ਮਈ।","roman":"Jih kee mukh upam chandraprabhaa jih kee tan bhaa mano roop maee |","meaning_en":"she whose face is likened to moonlight, whose body's glow seems made of beauty itself —","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਹ ਸੰਗ ਕੋ ਤ੍ਯਾਗਿ ਸੁਨੋ ਸਜਨੀ ਗ੍ਰਿਹ ਕੀ ਉਠ ਕੈ ਤੁਹਿ ਬਾਟ ਲਈ।","roman":"Tih sang ko tyaagi suno sajnee grih kee uth kai tuhi baat laee |","meaning_en":"leaving his company, listen, friend, you rose and took the road home;","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਨਾਥ ਕੇ ਸੰਗ ਸਖੀ ਬਹੁ ਤੇਰੀ ਰੀ ਤੋ ਸੀ ਗੁਵਾਰਿ ਭਈ ਨ ਭਈ। ੬੯੧।","roman":"Brij naath ke sang sakhee bahu teree ree to see guvaari bhaee na bhaee | 691 |","meaning_en":"the lord of Braj has many companions, but there has been no gopi like you, none at all.'","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਖੀ ਬਹੁ ਤੇਰੀ: read as 'many companions (like) you'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਕਬਿਯੋ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਕਬਿਯੋ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Kabiyo baach","meaning_en":"The poet said:","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[692],"number_text":"੬੯੨।","page":445,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨ ਕੈ ਇਹ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਕੀ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਮਨਿ ਕੋਪ ਭਈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Sun kai ih gvaarin kee bateeyaa brikhbhaan sutaa mani kop bhaee hai |","meaning_en":"Hearing these words of the gopi, Brikhbhan's daughter grew angry in her mind:","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਬਿਨਾ ਪਠਏ ਰੀ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਹਮਰੇ ਉਨ ਕੇ ਉਠਿ ਬੀਚ ਪਈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Kaanh binaa pathae ree treeyaa hamre un ke uthi beech paee hai |","meaning_en":"'Woman, without Kanh sending you, you have come and thrust yourself between him and me;","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਈ ਮਨਾਵਨ ਹੈ ਹਮ ਕੋ ਸੁ ਕਹੀ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਜੁ ਨਹੀ ਰੁਚਈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Aaee manaavan hai ham ko su kahee bateeyaa ju nahee ruchaee hai |","meaning_en":"you have come to win me over, and spoken words that do not please me.'","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੋਪ ਕੈ ਉਤਰ ਦੇਤ ਭਈ ਚਲ ਰੀ ਚਲ ਤੂ ਕਿਨਿ ਬੀਚ ਦਈ ਹੈ। ੬੯੨।","roman":"Kop kai utar det bhaee chal ree chal too kini beech daee hai | 692 |","meaning_en":"In anger she answered: 'Go, woman, go! Who asked you to come between us?'","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਦੂਤੀ ਬਾਚ ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਸੋ","gurmukhi":"ਦੂਤੀ ਬਾਚ ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਸੋ","roman":"Dootee baach kaanh so","meaning_en":"The messenger said to Kanh:","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[693],"number_text":"੬੯੩।","page":445,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕੋਪ ਕੈ ਉਤਰ ਦੇਤ ਭਈ ਇਨ ਆਇ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਫਿਰਿ ਸੰਗ ਸੁਜਾਨੈ।","roman":"Kop kai utar det bhaee in aai kahiyo phiri sang sujaanai |","meaning_en":"'She answered in anger,' this one came and said again to the wise one;","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁਜਾਨੈ: 'the wise one', Krishna."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੈਠ ਰਹੀ ਹਠ ਮਾਨਿ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਹਉ ਮਨਾਇ ਰਹੀ ਜੜ ਕਿਉ ਹੂੰ ਨ ਮਾਨੈ।","roman":"Baith rahee hath maani treeyaa hau manaai rahee jar kiu hoon na maanai |","meaning_en":"'the woman sits stubborn in her pique; I tried to win her over, but the foolish one will not agree at all;","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਮ ਦੀਏ ਨ ਮਨੈ ਨਹੀ ਦੰਡ ਮਨੈ ਨਹੀ ਭੇਦ ਦੀਏ ਅਰੁ ਦਾਨੈ।","roman":"Saam dee'e na manai nahee dand manai nahee bhed dee'e aru daanai |","meaning_en":"she does not yield to persuasion, nor to threat, nor to sowing doubt, nor to gifts;","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Sam, dand, bhed, daan: the four traditional means of persuasion."},{"gurmukhi":"ਐਸੀ ਗੁਵਾਰਿ ਸੋ ਹੇਤ ਕਹਾ ਤੁਮਰੀ ਜੋਊ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਕੋ ਰੰਗ ਨ ਜਾਨੈ। ੬੯੩।","roman":"Aisee guvaari so het kahaa tumree jo'oo preeti ko rang na jaanai | 693 |","meaning_en":"why love such a gopi, who does not know the colour of your love?'","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਮੈਨ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਬਾਚ ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਸੋ","gurmukhi":"ਮੈਨ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਬਾਚ ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਸੋ","roman":"Main prabhaa baach kaanh joo so","meaning_en":"Mainprabha said to Kanh:","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Name ਮੈਨ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ transliterated Mainprabha."},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[694],"number_text":"੬੯੪।","page":445,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੈਨ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਹਰਿ ਪਾਸ ਹੁਤੀ ਸੁਨ ਕੈ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਤਬ ਬੋਲਿ ਉਠੀ ਹੈ।","roman":"Main prabhaa hari paas hutee sun kai bateeyaa tab boli uthee hai |","meaning_en":"Mainprabha was near Krishna; hearing these words, she spoke up then:","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਿਆਇ ਹੋ ਹਉ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਤੁਮ ਤੇ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਜੋਊ ਗ੍ਵਾਰ ਰੁਠੀ ਹੈ।","roman":"Liaai ho hau ih bhaati kahiyo tum te hari joo jo'oo gvaar ruthee hai |","meaning_en":"'I will bring her,' so she said; 'Krishna, the gopi who is angry with you.'","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਕੇ ਪਾਇਨ ਪੈ ਤਬ ਹੀ ਸੁ ਲਿਯਾਵਨ ਤਾਹੀ ਕੇ ਕਾਜ ਉਠੀ ਹੈ।","roman":"Kaanh ke paain pai tab hee su liyaavan taahee ke kaaj uthee hai |","meaning_en":"Then, touching Kanh's feet, she rose at once to go and bring her;","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ ਮੁਖ ਊਪਰ ਤੇ ਮਨੋ ਕੰਜ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਸਭ ਵਾਰ ਸੁਟੀ ਹੈ। ੬੯੪।","roman":"Sundartaa mukh oopar te mano kanj prabhaa sabh vaar sutee hai | 694 |","meaning_en":"for the beauty of her face, it was as if all the splendour of the lotus had been offered up as a sacrifice.","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[695],"number_text":"੬੯੫।","page":445,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਰਿ ਪਾਇਨ ਪੈ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਉਹ ਕੇ ਢਿਗ ਹਉ ਚਲਿ ਜੈ ਹੋ।","roman":"Hari paain pai ih bhaati kahiyo hari joo uh ke dhig hau chali jai ho |","meaning_en":"Touching Krishna's feet, she said thus: 'Krishna, I will go to her;","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾ ਹੀ ਉਪਾਵ ਤੇ ਆਇ ਹੈ ਸੁੰਦਰਿ ਤਾਹੀ ਉਪਾਇ ਮਨਾਇ ਲਿਯੈ ਹੋ।","roman":"Jaa hee upaav te aai hai sundri taahee upaai manaai liyai ho |","meaning_en":"by whatever means the fair one will come, by that means I will win her over;","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਇਨ ਪੈ ਬਿਨਤੀਅਨ ਕੈ ਰਿਝਵਾਇ ਕੈ ਸੁੰਦਰਿ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿ ਮਨੈਹੋ।","roman":"Paain pai binteean kai rijhvaai kai sundri gvaari manaiho |","meaning_en":"falling at her feet, entreating and pleasing her, I will bring the lovely gopi round;","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਜ ਹੀ ਤੋ ਢਿਗ ਆਨਿ ਮਿਲੈਹੋ ਜੂ ਲ੍ਯਾਏ ਬਿਨਾ ਤੁਮਰੀ ਨ ਕਹੈ ਹੋ। ੬੯੫।","roman":"Aaj hee to dhig aani milaiho joo lyaae binaa tumree na kahai ho | 695 |","meaning_en":"this very day I will bring her to meet you; until I have brought her, I will not call myself yours.'","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Last clause read loosely; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[696],"number_text":"੬੯੬।","page":445,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਰਿ ਪਾਇਨ ਪੈ ਤਿਹ ਠਉਰ ਚਲੀ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਫੁਨਿ ਮੈਨ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ।","roman":"Hari paain pai tih thaur chalee kabi syaam kahai phuni main prabhaa |","meaning_en":"Touching Krishna's feet, Mainprabha then set out for that place, says the poet Shyam;","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਹ ਕੇ ਨਹੀ ਤੁਲਿ ਮੰਦੋਦਰਿ ਹੈ ਜਿਹ ਤੁਲ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਨਹੀ ਇੰਦ੍ਰ ਸਭਾ।","roman":"Jih ke nahee tuli mandodri hai jih tul treeyaa nahee indr sabhaa |","meaning_en":"she whom Mandodari does not equal, and whom no woman of Indra's court equals;","page":445,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਹ ਕੋ ਮੁਖ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਰਾਜਤ ਹੈ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਲਸੈ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਵਾ ਕੀ ਅਭਾ।","roman":"Jih ko mukh sundar raajat hai ih bhaati lasai treeyaa vaa kee abhaa |","meaning_en":"whose beautiful face shines, and whose radiance gleams thus:","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਨੋ ਚੰਦ ਕੁਰੰਗਨ ਕੇਹਰ ਕੀਰ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਕੋ ਸਭੋ ਧਨ ਯਾਹਿ ਲਭਾ। ੬੯੬।","roman":"Mano chand kurangan kehar keer prabhaa ko sabho dhan yaahi labhaa | 696 |","meaning_en":"as if she had gained all the wealth of splendour of the moon, the deer, the lion and the parrot.","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Traditional likenesses for face, eyes, waist and nose."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਪ੍ਰਤਿਉਤਰ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਤਿਉਤਰ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Pratiutar baach","meaning_en":"Reply:","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[697],"number_text":"੬੯੭।","page":446,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਲਿ ਚੰਦਮੁਖੀ ਹਰਿ ਕੇ ਢਿਗ ਤੇ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਪਹਿ ਪੈ ਚਲਿ ਆਈ।","roman":"Chali chandmukhee hari ke dhig te brikhbhaan sutaa pahi pai chali aaee |","meaning_en":"The moon-faced one went from Krishna's side and came to Brikhbhan's daughter;","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਇ ਕੈ ਐਸੇ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਤਿਹ ਸੋ ਬਲ ਬੇਗ ਚਲੋ ਨੰਦ ਲਾਲ ਬੁਲਾਈ।","roman":"Aai kai aise kahiyo tih so bal beg chalo nand laal bulaaee |","meaning_en":"coming, she said thus to her: 'Dear, come quickly, Nand's darling has called you.'","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੈ ਨ ਚਲੋ ਹਰਿ ਪਾਸ ਹਹਾ ਚਲੁ ਐਸੇ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਨ ਕਰੋ ਦੁਚਿਤਾਈ।","roman":"Mai na chalo hari paas hahaa chalu aise kahiyo na karo duchitaaee |","meaning_en":"'I will not go to Krishna.' 'Please, come; do not say so, do not be of two minds;","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Exchange read as Radha's refusal and Mainprabha's plea."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਹੇ ਕੋ ਬੈਠ ਰਹੀ ਇਹ ਠਉਰ ਮੈ ਮੋਹਨ ਕੋ ਮਨੋ ਚਿਤੁ ਚੁਰਾਈ। ੬੯੭।","roman":"Kaahe ko baith rahee ih thaur mai mohan ko mano chitu churaaee | 697 |","meaning_en":"why do you sit in this place, as if you had stolen Mohan's heart?'","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Mohan = Krishna."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[698],"number_text":"੬੯੮।","page":446,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਹਿ ਘੋਰ ਘਟਾ ਘਟ ਆਏ ਘਨੇ ਚਹੂੰ ਓਰਨ ਮੈ ਜਹ ਮੋਰ ਪੁਕਾਰੈ।","roman":"Jaahi ghor ghataa ghat aae ghane chahoon oran mai jah mor pukaarai |","meaning_en":"'Where dense, dark clouds have gathered on all four sides, where peacocks call,","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਾਚਤ ਹੈ ਜਹ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨੀਯਾ ਤਿਹ ਪੇਖਿ ਘਨੇ ਬਿਰਹੀ ਤਨ ਵਾਰੈ।","roman":"Naachat hai jah gvaarneeyaa tih pekhi ghane birhee tan vaarai |","meaning_en":"where the gopis dance, and seeing them many love-sick ones lay down their lives —","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਉਨ ਸਮੈ ਜਦੁਰਾਇ ਸੁਨੋ ਮੁਰਲੀ ਕੇ ਬਜਾਇ ਕੈ ਤੋਹਿ ਚਿਤਾਰੈ।","roman":"Taun samai jaduraai suno murlee ke bajaai kai tohi chitaarai |","meaning_en":"at that time, listen, the Yadav king plays the flute and thinks of you;","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਤੇ ਬੇਗ ਚਲੋ ਸਜਨੀ ਤਿਹ ਕਉਤਕ ਕੋ ਹਮ ਜਾਇ ਨਿਹਾਰੈ। ੬੯੮।","roman":"Taahee te beg chalo sajnee tih kautak ko ham jaai nihaarai | 698 |","meaning_en":"so come quickly, friend; let us go and watch that spectacle.'","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[699],"number_text":"੬੯੯।","page":446,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਤੇ ਨ ਮਾਨ ਕਰੋ ਸਜਨੀ ਹਰਿ ਪਾਸ ਚਲੋ ਨਾਹਿ ਸੰਕ ਬਿਚਾਰੋ।","roman":"Taa te na maan karo sajnee hari paas chalo naahi sank bichaaro |","meaning_en":"'So do not sulk, friend; go to Krishna and do not entertain doubts;","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਤ ਧਰੋ ਰਸ ਹੂੰ ਕੀ ਮਨੈ ਅਪਨੈ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਨ ਕਛੂ ਹਠ ਧਾਰੋ।","roman":"Baat dharo ras hoon kee manai apnai man mai na kachhoo hath dhaaro |","meaning_en":"keep in your heart thoughts of love, and hold no stubbornness in your mind;","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਉਤਕ ਕਾਨ ਕੋ ਦਖਨ ਕੋ ਤਿਹ ਕੋ ਜਸ ਪੈ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਉਚਾਰੋ।","roman":"Kautak kaan ko dakhan ko tih ko jas pai kabi syaam uchaaro |","meaning_en":"it is the spectacle of Kanh that I mean to see, whose praise the poet Shyam sings;","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Line read loosely; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਹੇ ਕਉ ਬੈਠ ਰਹੀ ਹਠ ਕੈ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਦੇਖਨ ਕਉ ਉਮਗਿਯੋ ਮਨ ਸਾਰੋ। ੬੯੯।","roman":"Kaahe kau baith rahee hath kai kahiyo dekhan kau umgiyo man saaro | 699 |","meaning_en":"why do you sit there stubbornly?' she said; 'my whole heart is eager to see it.'","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[700],"number_text":"੭੦੦।","page":446,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਰਿ ਪਾਸ ਨ ਮੈ ਚਲਹੋ ਸਜਨੀ ਪਿਖਬੇ ਕਹੁ ਕਉਤੁਕ ਜੀਯ ਨ ਮੇਰੋ।","roman":"Hari paas na mai chalho sajnee pikhbe kahu kautuk jeey na mero |","meaning_en":"'I will not go to Krishna, friend; my heart has no wish to see the spectacle;","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਰਚੇ ਸੰਗ ਅਉਰ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਤਜ ਕੈ ਹਮ ਸੋ ਫੁਨਿ ਨੇਹ ਘਨੇਰੋ।","roman":"Syaam rache sang aur treeyaa taj kai ham so phuni neh ghanero |","meaning_en":"Shyam has given himself to another woman, after first loving me so deeply;","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚੰਦ੍ਰਭਗਾ ਹੂੰ ਕੇ ਸੰਗਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਨਹਿ ਨਾਰੀ ਕਹਾ ਮੁਹਿ ਨੈਨਨ ਹੇਰੋ।","roman":"Chandrabhgaa hoon ke sangi kahiyo nahi naaree kahaa muhi nainan hero |","meaning_en":"he spoke with Chandrabhaga; he did not even look at me with his eyes, woman;","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Line read loosely; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਤੇ ਨ ਪਾਸ ਚਲੋ ਹਰਿ ਹਉ ਉਠਿ ਜਾਹਿ ਜੋਊ ਉਮਗਿਯੋ ਮਨ ਤੇਰੋ। ੭੦੦।","roman":"Taa te na paas chalo hari hau uthi jaahi jo'oo umgiyo man tero | 700 |","meaning_en":"so I will not go to Krishna; you rise and go, if your heart is so eager.'","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਦੂਤੀ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਦੂਤੀ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Dootee baach","meaning_en":"The messenger said:","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[701],"number_text":"੭੦੧।","page":446,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੈ ਕਹਾ ਦੇਖਨ ਜਾਉ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਤੁਹਿ ਲ੍ਯਾਵਨ ਕੋ ਜਦੁਰਾਇ ਪਠਾਈ।","roman":"Mai kahaa dekhan jaau treeyaa tuhi lyaavan ko jaduraai pathaaee |","meaning_en":"'Why would I go to watch? Woman, the Yadav king sent me to fetch you;","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਤੇ ਹਉ ਸਭ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਤੇ ਉਠ ਕੈ ਤਬ ਹੀ ਤੁਮਰੇ ਪਹਿ ਆਈ।","roman":"Taahee te hau sabh gvaarni te uth kai tab hee tumre pahi aaee |","meaning_en":"that is why I rose from among all the gopis and came straight to you;","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੂ ਅਭਿਮਾਨ ਕੈ ਬੈਠ ਰਹੀ ਨਹੀ ਮਾਨਤ ਹੈ ਕਛੂ ਸੀਖ ਪਰਾਈ।","roman":"Too abhimaan kai baith rahee nahee maanat hai kachhoo seekh paraaee |","meaning_en":"you sit there in your pride and accept no one else's advice at all;","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੇਗ ਚਲੋ ਤੁਹਿ ਸੰਗ ਕਹੋ ਤੁਮਰੇ ਮਗੁ ਹੇਰਤ ਠਾਢਿ ਕਨ੍ਹਾਈ। ੭੦੧।","roman":"Beg chalo tuhi sang kaho tumre magu herat thaadhi kanhaaee | 701 |","meaning_en":"come quickly, I tell you; Kanhai stands watching the road for you.'","page":446,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Raadhe baach","meaning_en":"Radha said:","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[702],"number_text":"੭੦੨।","page":447,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਰਿ ਪਾਸ ਨ ਮੈ ਚਲਹੋ ਰੀ ਸਖੀ ਤੁ ਕਹਾ ਭਯੋ ਜੁ ਤੁਹਿ ਬਾਤ ਬਨਾਈ।","roman":"Hari paas na mai chalho ree sakhee tu kahaa bhayo ju tuhi baat banaaee |","meaning_en":"'I will not go to Krishna, friend; what of it that you have made up this tale?","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਨ ਮੋਰੇ ਤੂ ਪਾਸ ਪਠੀ ਇਹ ਬਾਤਨ ਤੇ ਕਪਟੀ ਲਖਿ ਪਾਈ।","roman":"Syaam na more too paas pathee ih baatan te kaptee lakhi paaee |","meaning_en":"Shyam did not send you to me; from these words I can see you are deceitful.'","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭੀ ਕਪਟੀ ਤੁ ਕਹਾ ਭਯੋ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਤੂ ਨ ਲਖੈ ਕਛੁ ਪੀਰ ਪਰਾਈ।","roman":"Bhee kaptee tu kahaa bhayo gvaarni too na lakhai kachhu peer paraaee |","meaning_en":"'What if I am deceitful, gopi? You know nothing of another's pain.'","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Speaker read as the messenger; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਕਹਿ ਕੈ ਸਿਰ ਨ੍ਯਾਇ ਰਹੀ ਕਹਿ ਐਸੋ ਨ ਮਾਨ ਪਿਖਿਯੋ ਕਹੂੰ ਮਾਈ। ੭੦੨।","roman":"Yau kahi kai sir nyaai rahee kahi aiso na maan pikhiyo kahoon maaee | 702 |","meaning_en":"Saying this, she sat with bowed head and said, 'Mother, I have never seen such pique anywhere.'","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਦੂਤੀ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਦੂਤੀ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Dootee baach","meaning_en":"The messenger said:","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[703],"number_text":"੭੦੩।","page":447,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਫਿਰਿ ਐਸੇ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਚਲੀਯੇ ਰੀ ਹਹਾ ਬਲ ਮੈ ਹਰਿ ਕੇ ਪਹਿ ਯੋ ਕਹਿ ਆਈ।","roman":"Phiri aise kahiyo chaleeye ree hahaa bal mai hari ke pahi yo kahi aaee |","meaning_en":"Then she said thus: 'Come, I beg you, dear; I came here after saying this to Krishna:","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋਹੁ ਨ ਆਤੁਰ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਬ੍ਰਿਜਨਾਥ ਹਉ ਲ੍ਯਾਵਤ ਹੋ ਉਹਿ ਜਾਇ ਮਨਾਈ।","roman":"Hohu na aatur sree brijnaath hau lyaavat ho uhi jaai manaaee |","meaning_en":"\"Do not be anxious, revered lord of Braj; I will go, win her over and bring her.\"","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਇਤ ਤੂ ਕਰਿ ਮਾਨ ਰਹੀ ਸਜਨੀ ਹਰਿ ਪੈ ਤੁ ਚਲੋ ਤਜਿ ਕੈ ਦੁਚਿਤਾਈ।","roman":"It too kari maan rahee sajnee hari pai tu chalo taji kai duchitaaee |","meaning_en":"Here you sit in pique, friend; leave your doubts and come to Krishna;","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੋ ਬਿਨੁ ਮੋ ਪੈ ਨ ਜਾਤ ਗਯੋ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਜਾਨਤ ਹੈ ਕਛੁ ਬਾਤ ਪਰਾਈ। ੭੦੩।","roman":"To binu mo pai na jaat gayo kahiyo jaanat hai kachhu baat paraaee | 703 |","meaning_en":"without you I cannot go back to him.' She said: 'You know something of another's heart.'","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Second clause read loosely; uncertain."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Raadhe baach","meaning_en":"Radha said:","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[704],"number_text":"੭੦੪।","page":447,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਉਠ ਆਈ ਹੁਤੀ ਤੁ ਕਹਾ ਭਯੋ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਆਈ ਨ ਪੂਛਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਕਛੁ ਸੋਰੀ।","roman":"Uth aaee hutee tu kahaa bhayo gvaarni aaee na poochhi kahiyo kachhu soree |","meaning_en":"'What if you got up and came, gopi? You did not come asking my leave, nor say anything to me;","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੋਰੀ: read loosely; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਹਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਫਿਰਿ ਕੈ ਹਰਿ ਪੈ ਇਹ ਤੇ ਕਛੁ ਲਾਜ ਨ ਲਾਗਤ ਤੋਰੀ।","roman":"Jaahi kahiyo phiri kai hari pai ih te kachhu laaj na laagat toree |","meaning_en":"go back to Krishna, I say; do you feel no shame in this?","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੋ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਜਦੁਰਾਇ ਜੁ ਪੈ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਕਹੀਯੋ ਸੁ ਅਹੋ ਰੀ।","roman":"Mo bateeyaa jaduraai ju pai kabi syaam kahai kaheeyo su aho ree |","meaning_en":"my words to the Yadav king, says the poet Shyam, tell him thus, I say:","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚੰਦ੍ਰਭਗਾ ਸੰਗਿ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਕਰੋ ਤੁਮ ਸੋ ਨਹੀ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਪ੍ਰਭ ਮੋਰੀ। ੭੦੪।","roman":"Chandrabhgaa sangi preeti karo tum so nahee preeti kahiyo prabh moree | 704 |","meaning_en":"\"Make love with Chandrabhaga; my lord has no love for you,\" she said.'","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Read as Radha's message: 'my lord, I have no love for you'; the exact sense of 'ਤੁਮ ਸੋ ਨਹੀ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ... ਪ੍ਰਭ ਮੋਰੀ' is uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[705],"number_text":"੭੦੫।","page":447,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨਿ ਕੈ ਇਹ ਰਾਧਿਕਾ ਕੀ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਤਬ ਸੋ ਉਠਿ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਪਾਇ ਲਾਗੀ।","roman":"Suni kai ih raadhikaa kee bateeyaa tab so uthi gvaarni paai laagee |","meaning_en":"Hearing these words of Radhika, the gopi then rose and touched her feet:","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਹਰਿ ਕੀ ਤੁਮ ਸੋ ਹਰਿ ਚੰਦ੍ਰਭਗਾ ਹੂੰ ਸੋ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਤਿਯਾਗੀ।","roman":"Preeti kahiyo hari kee tum so hari chandrabhgaa hoon so preeti tiyaagee |","meaning_en":"'Krishna's love is for you,' she said; 'Krishna has given up his love for Chandrabhaga;","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਉਨ ਕੀ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਸੁਬੁਧਿ ਕਹੈ ਤੁਹਿ ਦੇਖਨ ਕੇ ਰਸ ਮੈ ਅਨੁਰਾਗੀ।","roman":"Un kee kabi syaam subudhi kahai tuhi dekhan ke ras mai anuraagee |","meaning_en":"his good mind, says the poet Shyam, is in love with the delight of seeing you;","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਤੇ ਬਾਲ ਬਲਾਇ ਲਿਉ ਤੇਰੀ ਮੈ ਬੇਗ ਚਲੋ ਹਰਿ ਪੈ ਬਡਭਾਗੀ। ੭੦੫।","roman":"Taahee te baal balaai liu teree mai beg chalo hari pai badbhaagee | 705 |","meaning_en":"so, girl, may I take your troubles on me; go quickly to Krishna, fortunate one.'","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[706],"number_text":"੭੦੬।","page":447,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਨਾਥ ਬੁਲਾਵਤ ਹੈ ਚਲੀਯੈ ਕਛੁ ਜਾਨਤ ਹੈ ਰਸ ਬਾਤ ਇਯਾਨੀ।","roman":"Brij naath bulaavat hai chaleeyai kachhu jaanat hai ras baat iyaanee |","meaning_en":"'The lord of Braj is calling; come; you know little of the ways of love, innocent one;","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਇਯਾਨੀ: 'innocent, childish'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੋਹੀ ਕੋ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਨਿਹਾਰਤ ਹੈ ਤੁਮਰੈ ਬਿਨੁ ਰੀ ਨਹੀ ਪੀਵਤ ਪਾਨੀ।","roman":"Tohee ko syaam nihaarat hai tumrai binu ree nahee peevat paanee |","meaning_en":"it is you that Shyam is looking for; without you he does not even drink water;","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੂ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਕਹੈ ਮੁਖ ਤੇ ਨਹੀ ਜਾਊਗੀ ਹਉ ਹਰਿ ਪੈ ਇਹ ਬਾਨੀ।","roman":"Too ih bhaati kahai mukh te nahee jaaoogee hau hari pai ih baanee |","meaning_en":"and you say with your mouth these words: \"I will not go to Krishna\";","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਤੇ ਜਾਨਤ ਹੋ ਸਜਨੀ ਅਬ ਜੋਬਨ ਪਾਇ ਭਈ ਹੈ ਦੀਵਾਨੀ। ੭੦੬।","roman":"Taahee te jaanat ho sajnee ab joban paai bhaee hai deevaanee | 706 |","meaning_en":"from this I know, friend, that having come into youth you have gone mad.'","page":447,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[707],"number_text":"੭੦੭।","page":448,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਨ ਕਰਿਯੋ ਮਨ ਬੀਚ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਤਜਿ ਬੈਠਿ ਰਹੀ ਹਿਤ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਜੂ ਕੇਰੋ।","roman":"Maan kariyo man beech treeyaa taji baithi rahee hit syaam joo kero |","meaning_en":"'Woman, you have taken pique in your heart and sit here, giving up Shyam's love;","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੈਠਿ ਰਹੀ ਬਕ ਧ੍ਯਾਨ ਧਰੇ ਸਭ ਜਾਨਤ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਕੋ ਭਾਵਨ ਨੇਰੋ।","roman":"Baithi rahee bak dhyaan dhare sabh jaanat preeti ko bhaavan nero |","meaning_en":"you sit like a heron feigning meditation; everyone knows how close you are in love;","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਕ ਧ੍ਯਾਨ: 'heron's meditation', a show of stillness; line read loosely."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੋ ਸੰਗ ਤੌ ਮੈ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਸਜਨੀ ਕਹਬੇ ਕਹੁ ਜੋ ਉਮਗਿਯੋ ਮਨ ਮੇਰੋ।","roman":"To sang tau mai kahiyo sajnee kahbe kahu jo umgiyo man mero |","meaning_en":"I have told you, friend, what my heart was eager to say:","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਵਤ ਹੈ ਇਮ ਮੋ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਦਿਨ ਚਾਰ ਕੋ ਪਾਹੁਨੋ ਜੋਬਨ ਤੇਰੋ। ੭੦੭।","roman":"Aavat hai im mo man mai din chaar ko paahuno joban tero | 707 |","meaning_en":"this comes to my mind, that your youth is a guest of only four days.'","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[708],"number_text":"੭੦੮।","page":448,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਕੈ ਨ ਪਾਸ ਚਲੈ ਉਠ ਕੈ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਜੋਊ ਸਭ ਲੋਗਨ ਭੋਗੀ।","roman":"Taa kai na paas chalai uth kai kabi syaam jo'oo sabh logan bhogee |","meaning_en":"'You do not rise and go to him, says the poet Shyam, who is the enjoyer of all people;","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਤੇ ਰਹੀ ਹਠਿ ਬੈਠ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਉਨ ਕੋ ਕਛੁ ਜੈ ਗੋ ਨ ਆਪਨ ਖੋਗੀ।","roman":"Taa te rahee hathi baith treeyaa un ko kachhu jai go na aapan khogee |","meaning_en":"so you sit there stubborn, woman; he will lose nothing, you will lose your own;","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋਬਨ ਕੋ ਜੁ ਗੁਮਾਨ ਕਰੈ ਤਿਹ ਜੋਬਨ ਕੀ ਸੁ ਦਸਾ ਇਹ ਹੋਗੀ।","roman":"Joban ko ju gumaan karai tih joban kee su dasaa ih hogee |","meaning_en":"she who is proud of her youth, this will be the state of that youth:","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੋ ਤਜਿ ਕੈ ਸੋਊ ਯੋ ਰਮਿ ਹੈ ਜਿਮ ਕੰਧ ਪੈ ਡਾਰ ਬਘੰਬਰ ਜੋਗੀ। ੭੦੮।","roman":"To taji kai so'oo yo rami hai jim kandh pai daar baghanbar jogee | 708 |","meaning_en":"he will leave you and roam like a yogi with a tiger-skin thrown over his shoulder.'","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[709],"number_text":"੭੦੯।","page":448,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨੈਨ ਕੁਰੰਗਨ ਸੇ ਤੁਮਰੇ ਕੇਹਰਿ ਕੀ ਕਟਿ ਰੀ ਸੁਨ ਤ੍ਵੈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Nain kurangan se tumre kehri kee kati ree sun tvai hai |","meaning_en":"'Your eyes are like a deer's, and listen, your waist is like a lion's;","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਨਨ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਹੈ ਸਸਿ ਸੋ ਜਿਹ ਕੀ ਫੁਨਿ ਕੰਜ ਬਰਾਬਰ ਕ੍ਵੈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Aanan sundar hai sasi so jih kee phuni kanj baraabar kvai hai |","meaning_en":"your face is beautiful like the moon; what lotus can equal it?","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੈਠ ਰਹੀ ਹਠ ਬਾਧਿ ਘਨੋ ਤਿਹ ਤੇ ਕਛੁ ਆਪਨ ਹੀ ਸੁਨ ਖ੍ਵੈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Baith rahee hath baadhi ghano tih te kachhu aapan hee sun khvai hai |","meaning_en":"you sit binding yourself in great stubbornness; listen, by this you will lose something of your own;","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਏ ਤਨ ਸੁ ਤੁਹਿ ਬੈਰ ਕਰਿਯੋ ਹਰਿ ਸਿਉ ਹਠਿਏ ਤੁਮਰੋ ਕਹੁ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਹੈ। ੭੦੯।","roman":"E tan su tuhi bair kariyo hari siu hathie tumro kahu hvai hai | 709 |","meaning_en":"you have made enmity with Krishna; stubborn one, what will become of you?'","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਏ ਤਨ ਸੁ ਤੁਹਿ: read loosely; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[710],"number_text":"੭੧੦।","page":448,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨ ਕੈ ਇਹ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਕੀ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਅਤਿ ਰੋਸ ਭਰੀ।","roman":"Sun kai ih gvaarni kee bateeyaa brikhbhaan sutaa ati ros bharee |","meaning_en":"Hearing these words of the gopi, Brikhbhan's daughter was filled with great anger;","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨੈਨ ਨਚਾਇ ਚੜਾਇ ਕੈ ਭਉਹਨ ਪੈ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਸੰਗ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਜਰੀ।","roman":"Nain nachaai charaai kai bhauhan pai man mai sang krodh jaree |","meaning_en":"rolling her eyes and raising her brows, she burned with wrath in her heart;","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋਊ ਆਈ ਮਨਾਵਨ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਥੀ ਤਿਹ ਸੋ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਇਮ ਪੈ ਉਚਰੀ।","roman":"Jo'oo aaee manaavan gvaarni thee tih so bateeyaa im pai uchree |","meaning_en":"to the gopi who had come to win her over, she spoke these words:","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਖੀ ਕਾਹੇ ਕੌ ਹਉ ਹਰਿ ਪਾਸ ਚਲੋ ਹਰਿ ਕੀ ਕਛੁ ਮੋ ਪਰਵਾਹ ਪਰੀ। ੭੧੦।","roman":"Sakhee kaahe kau hau hari paas chalo hari kee kachhu mo parvaah paree | 710 |","meaning_en":"'Friend, why should I go to Krishna? What do I care for Krishna?'","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[711],"number_text":"੭੧੧।","page":448,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਇਹ ਉਤਰ ਦੇਤ ਭਈ ਤਬ ਯਾ ਬਿਧਿ ਸੋ ਉਨਿ ਬਾਤ ਕਰੀ ਹੈ।","roman":"Yau ih utar det bhaee tab yaa bidhi so uni baat karee hai |","meaning_en":"She gave this answer; then the other spoke in this way:","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਲਾਇ ਲਿਉ ਰੋਸ ਕਰੋ ਨਹਿ ਕਿਉ ਕਿਹ ਕੋਪ ਕੇ ਸੰਗ ਭਰੀ ਹੈ।","roman":"Raadhe balaai liu ros karo nahi kiu kih kop ke sang bharee hai |","meaning_en":"'Radha, may I take your troubles on me, do not be angry; why are you so filled with wrath?","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੂ ਇਤ ਮਾਨ ਰਹੀ ਕਰਿ ਕੈ ਉਤ ਹੇਰਤ ਪੈ ਰਿਪੁ ਚੰਦ ਹਰੀ ਹੈ।","roman":"Too it maan rahee kari kai ut herat pai ripu chand haree hai |","meaning_en":"you sit here in pique, while there Krishna, the foe of the moon, looks out for you;","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰਿਪੁ ਚੰਦ: 'foe of the moon', i.e. one whose face outshines the moon; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੂ ਨ ਕਰੈ ਪਰਵਾਹ ਹਰੀ ਹਰਿ ਕੌ ਤੁਮਰੀ ਪਰਵਾਹ ਪਰੀ ਹੈ। ੭੧੧।","roman":"Too na karai parvaah haree hari kau tumree parvaah paree hai | 711 |","meaning_en":"you do not care for Krishna, but Krishna cares for you.'","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[712],"number_text":"੭੧੨।","page":448,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੋ ਕਹਿ ਬਾਤ ਕਹੀ ਫਿਰਿ ਯੌ ਉਠਿ ਬੇਗ ਚਲੋ ਚਲਿ ਹੋਹੁ ਸੰਜੋਗੀ।","roman":"Yo kahi baat kahee phiri yau uthi beg chalo chali hohu sanjogee |","meaning_en":"Having said this, she spoke again thus: 'Rise and come quickly, come and be united;","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਕੇ ਨੈਨ ਲਗੇ ਇਹ ਠਉਰ ਜੋਊ ਸਭ ਲੋਗਨ ਕੋ ਰਸ ਭੋਗੀ।","roman":"Taahee ke nain lage ih thaur jo'oo sabh logan ko ras bhogee |","meaning_en":"his eyes are fixed on this place, he who is the enjoyer of all people's love;","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਕੇ ਨ ਪਾਸ ਚਲੈ ਸਜਨੀ ਉਨ ਕੋ ਕਛ ਜੈ ਹੈ ਨ ਆਪਨ ਖੋਗੀ।","roman":"Taa ke na paas chalai sajnee un ko kachh jai hai na aapan khogee |","meaning_en":"if you do not go to him, friend, he will lose nothing; you will lose your own;","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੈ ਮੁਖ ਰੀ ਬਲਿ ਦੇਖਨ ਕੋ ਜਦੁਰਾਇ ਕੇ ਨੈਨ ਭਏ ਦੋਊ ਬਿਓਗੀ। ੭੧੨।","roman":"Tai mukh ree bali dekhan ko jaduraai ke nain bhae do'oo biogee | 712 |","meaning_en":"dear, both the Yadav king's eyes are pining to see your face.'","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[713],"number_text":"੭੧੩।","page":448,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪੇਖਤ ਹੈ ਨਹੀ ਅਉਰ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਤੁਮਰੋ ਈ ਸੁਨੋ ਬਲਿ ਪੰਥ ਨਿਹਾਰੈ।","roman":"Pekhat hai nahee aur treeyaa tumro ee suno bali panth nihaarai |","meaning_en":"'He looks at no other woman; listen, dear, he watches only your road;","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੇਰੇ ਹੀ ਧ੍ਯਾਨ ਬਿਖੈ ਅਟਕੇ ਤੁਮਰੀ ਹੀ ਕਿਧੌ ਬਲਿ ਬਾਤ ਉਚਾਰੈ।","roman":"Tere hee dhyaan bikhai atke tumree hee kidhau bali baat uchaarai |","meaning_en":"he is caught up in thinking of you alone, and, dear, speaks only of you;","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਝੂਮਿ ਗਿਰੈ ਕਬਹੂੰ ਧਰਨੀ ਕਰਿ ਤ੍ਵੈ ਮਧਿ ਆਪਨ ਆਪ ਸੰਭਾਰੈ।","roman":"Jhoomi girai kabhoon dharnee kari tvai madhi aapan aap sanbhaarai |","meaning_en":"sometimes he swoons and falls to the ground, and in thought of you steadies himself;","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਰਿ ਤ੍ਵੈ ਮਧਿ: read loosely; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਉਨ ਸਮੈ ਸਖੀ ਤੋਹਿ ਚਿਤਾਰਿ ਕੈ ਸ੍ਯਾਮਿ ਜੂ ਮੈਨ ਕੋ ਮਾਨ ਨਿਵਾਰੈ। ੭੧੩।","roman":"Taun samai sakhee tohi chitaari kai syaami joo main ko maan nivaarai | 713 |","meaning_en":"at that time, friend, remembering you, Shyam puts down the pride of Kamdev.'","page":448,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[714],"number_text":"੭੧੪।","page":449,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਤੇ ਨ ਮਾਨ ਕਰੋ ਸਜਨੀ ਉਠਿ ਬੇਗ ਚਲੋ ਕਛੁ ਸੰਕ ਨ ਆਨੋ।","roman":"Taa te na maan karo sajnee uthi beg chalo kachhu sank na aano |","meaning_en":"'So do not sulk, friend; rise and come quickly; have no doubt;","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕੀ ਬਾਤ ਸੁਨੋ ਹਮ ਤੇ ਤੁਮਰੇ ਚਿਤ ਮੈ ਅਪਨੋ ਚਿਤ ਮਾਨੋ।","roman":"Syaam kee baat suno ham te tumre chit mai apno chit maano |","meaning_en":"hear Shyam's word from me: consider his heart as one with your heart;","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੇਰੇ ਹੀ ਧ੍ਯਾਨ ਫਸੇ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਕਰ ਕੈ ਮਨਿ ਸੋਕ ਅਸੋਕ ਬਹਾਨੋ।","roman":"Tere hee dhyaan phase hari joo kar kai mani sok asok bahaano |","meaning_en":"Krishna is caught in thought of you, making sorrow of heart his excuse for being without sorrow;","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੋਕ ਅਸੋਕ ਬਹਾਨੋ: unclear phrase; read loosely; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੂੜ ਰਹੀ ਅਬਲਾ ਕਰਿ ਮਾਨ ਕਛੁ ਹਰਿ ਕੋ ਨਹੀ ਹੇਤ ਪਛਾਨੋ। ੭੧੪।","roman":"Moor rahee ablaa kari maan kachhu hari ko nahee het pachhaano | 714 |","meaning_en":"foolish girl, you sit in pique and do not recognise Krishna's love at all.'","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[715],"number_text":"੭੧੫।","page":449,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਕੀ ਸੁਨ ਕੈ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਤਬ ਰਾਧਿਕਾ ਉਤਰ ਦੇਤ ਭਈ।","roman":"Gvaarni kee sun kai bateeyaa tab raadhikaa utar det bhaee |","meaning_en":"Hearing the gopi's words, Radhika then gave this answer:","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਹ ਹੇਤ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਤਜਿ ਕੈ ਹਰਿ ਪਾਸਿ ਮਨਾਵਨ ਮੋਹੂ ਕੇ ਕਾਜ ਧਈ।","roman":"Kih het kahiyo taji kai hari paasi manaavan mohoo ke kaaj dhaee |","meaning_en":"'Why,' she said, 'did you leave Krishna's side and run here to win me over?","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਹਿ ਹਉ ਚਲਿ ਹੋ ਹਰਿ ਪਾਸ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਤੁਮਰੀ ਧਉ ਕਹਾ ਗਤਿ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਹੈ ਦਈ।","roman":"Nahi hau chali ho hari paas kahiyo tumree dhau kahaa gati hvai hai daee |","meaning_en":"I will not go to Krishna,' she said; 'God knows what will become of you;","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਧਉ ... ਦਈ: read as 'God (Daiv) knows'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਖੀ ਅਉਰਨ ਨਾਮ ਸੁ ਮੂੜ ਧਰੈ ਨ ਲਖੈ ਇਹ ਹਉ ਹੂੰ ਕਿ ਮੂੜ ਮਈ। ੭੧੫।","roman":"Sakhee auran naam su moor dharai na lakhai ih hau hoon ki moor maee | 715 |","meaning_en":"friend, you call others fools, but do not see whether I am the fool or you.'","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Line read loosely; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[716],"number_text":"੭੧੬।","page":449,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨ ਕੈ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਕੋ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਸੋ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਉਤਰ ਦੀਨੋ।","roman":"Sun kai brikhbhaan sutaa ko kahiyo ih bhaati so gvaarni utar deeno |","meaning_en":"Hearing what Brikhbhan's daughter said, the gopi answered in this way:","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੀ ਸੁਨ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਮੋ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਤਿਨ ਹੂੰ ਸੁਨਿ ਸ੍ਰੌਨ ਸੁਨੈਬੇ ਕਉ ਕੀਨੋ।","roman":"Ree sun gvaarni mo bateeyaa tin hoon suni sraun sunaibe kau keeno |","meaning_en":"'Listen, gopi, to my words,' — she made her hear them with her ears —","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Line read loosely; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੋਹਿ ਕਹੈ ਮੁਖ ਤੇ ਕਿ ਤੂ ਮੂੜ ਮੈ ਮੂੜ ਤੁਹੀ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਕਰਿ ਚੀਨੋ।","roman":"Mohi kahai mukh te ki too moor mai moor tuhee man mai kari cheeno |","meaning_en":"'you call me a fool to my face; know in your heart that the fool is you;","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੈ ਜਦੁਰਾਇ ਕੀ ਭੇਜੀ ਅਈ ਸੁਨਿ ਤੈ ਜਦੁਰਾਇ ਹੂੰ ਸੋ ਹਠ ਕੀਨੋ। ੭੧੬।","roman":"Jai jaduraai kee bhejee aee suni tai jaduraai hoon so hath keeno | 716 |","meaning_en":"I came sent by the Yadav king, and you have been stubborn even with the Yadav king.'","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[717],"number_text":"੭੧੭।","page":449,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਕਹਿ ਕੈ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਚਲੀਯੈ ਉਠਿ ਕੈ ਬਲਿ ਸੰਕ ਨ ਆਨੋ।","roman":"Yau kahi kai ih bhaati kahiyo chaleeyai uthi kai bali sank na aano |","meaning_en":"Having said this, she spoke thus: 'Rise and come, dear, have no doubt;","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੋ ਹੀ ਸੋ ਹੇਤੁ ਘਨੋ ਹਰਿ ਕੋ ਤਿਹ ਤੇ ਤੁਮ ਹੂੰ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਸਾਚ ਹੀ ਜਾਨੋ।","roman":"To hee so hetu ghano hari ko tih te tum hoon kahiyo saach hee jaano |","meaning_en":"Krishna's love is great for you alone; take what I say as the truth;","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਇਨ ਤੋਰੇ ਪਰੋ ਲਲਨਾ ਹਠ ਦੂਰ ਕਰੋ ਕਬਹੂੰ ਫੁਨਿ ਮਾਨੋ।","roman":"Paain tore paro lalnaa hath door karo kabhoon phuni maano |","meaning_en":"I fall at your feet, dear one; put away your stubbornness and for once agree;","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਤੇ ਨਿਸੰਕ ਚਲੋ ਤਜਿ ਸੰਕ ਕਿਧੌ ਹਰਿ ਕੀ ਵਹ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਪਛਾਨੋ। ੭੧੭।","roman":"Taa te nisank chalo taji sank kidhau hari kee vah preeti pachhaano | 717 |","meaning_en":"so go without fear, leaving doubt, and recognise that love of Krishna.'","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[718],"number_text":"੭੧੮।","page":449,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕੁੰਜਨ ਮੈ ਸਖੀ ਰਾਸ ਸਮੈ ਹਰਿ ਕੇਲ ਕਰੇ ਤੁਮ ਸੋ ਬਨ ਮੈ।","roman":"Kunjan mai sakhee raas samai hari kel kare tum so ban mai |","meaning_en":"'Friend, in the arbours, at the time of the Ras, Krishna played with you in the forest;","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਤਨੋ ਉਨ ਕੋ ਹਿਤ ਹੈ ਤੁਹਿ ਮੋ ਤਿਹ ਤੇ ਨਹੀ ਆਧਿਕ ਹੈ ਉਨ ਮੈ।","roman":"Jitno un ko hit hai tuhi mo tih te nahee aadhik hai un mai |","meaning_en":"as much love as he has for you, he has not more for any of them;","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੁਰਝਾਇ ਗਏ ਬਿਨੁ ਤੈ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਨਹਿ ਖੇਲਤ ਹੈ ਫੁਨਿ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨ ਮੈ।","roman":"Murjhaai gae binu tai hari joo nahi khelat hai phuni gvaarin mai |","meaning_en":"without you Krishna has wilted, and no longer plays among the gopis;","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਹ ਤੇ ਸੁਨ ਬੇਗ ਨਿਸੰਕ ਚਲੋ ਕਰ ਕੈ ਸੁਧਿ ਪੈ ਬਨ ਕੀ ਮਨ ਮੈ। ੭੧੮।","roman":"Tih te sun beg nisank chalo kar kai sudhi pai ban kee man mai | 718 |","meaning_en":"so listen, come quickly and fearlessly, remembering in your heart the forest.'","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[719],"number_text":"੭੧੯।","page":449,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਬੁਲਾਵਤ ਹੈ ਚਲੀਯੈ ਬਲਿ ਬਲਿ ਪੈ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਨ ਕਛੁ ਹਠੁ ਕੀਜੈ।","roman":"Syaam bulaavat hai chaleeyai bali bali pai man mai na kachhu hathu keejai |","meaning_en":"'Shyam is calling; come, dear, I am devoted to you; do not be stubborn at heart;","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਲਿ ਬਲਿ: 'I am a sacrifice to you'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੈਠ ਰਹੀ ਕਰਿ ਮਾਨ ਘਨੋ ਕਛੁ ਅਉਰਨ ਹੂੰ ਕੋ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਸੁਨ ਲੀਜੈ।","roman":"Baith rahee kari maan ghano kachhu auran hoon ko kahiyo sun leejai |","meaning_en":"you sit in great pique; listen a little to what others say;","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਤੇ ਹਉ ਬਾਤ ਕਰੋ ਤੁਮ ਸੋ ਇਹ ਤੇ ਨ ਕਛੂ ਤੁਮਰੋ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਛੀਜੈ।","roman":"Taa te hau baat karo tum so ih te na kachhoo tumro kahiyo chheejai |","meaning_en":"that is why I talk with you; nothing of yours is lost by doing as I say;","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨੈਕੁ ਨਿਹਾਰ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਹਮ ਓਰਿ ਸਭੈ ਤਜ ਮਾਨ ਅਬੈ ਹਸਿ ਦੀਜੈ। ੭੧੯।","roman":"Naiku nihaar kahiyo ham ori sabhai taj maan abai hasi deejai | 719 |","meaning_en":"look this way at me a little,' she said; 'give up all pique and smile now.'","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ ਦੂਤੀ ਸੋ","gurmukhi":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ ਦੂਤੀ ਸੋ","roman":"Raadhe baach dootee so","meaning_en":"Radha said to the messenger:","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[720],"number_text":"੭੨੦।","page":449,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੈ ਨ ਹਸੋ ਹਰਿ ਪਾਸ ਚਲੋ ਨਹੀ ਜਉ ਤੁਹਿ ਸੀ ਸਖੀ ਕੋਟਿਕ ਆਵੈ।","roman":"Mai na haso hari paas chalo nahee jau tuhi see sakhee kotik aavai |","meaning_en":"'I will not smile, and I will not go to Krishna, even if ten million friends like you come;","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਇ ਉਪਾਵ ਅਨੇਕ ਕਰੈ ਅਰੁ ਪਾਇਨ ਊਪਰ ਸੀਸ ਨਿਆਵੈ।","roman":"Aai upaav anek karai aru paain oopar sees niaavai |","meaning_en":"even if they come and try countless ways, and bow their heads at my feet;","page":449,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੈ ਕਬਹੂ ਨਹੀ ਜਾਉ ਤਹਾ ਤੁਹ ਸੀ ਕਹਿ ਕੋਟਿਕ ਬਾਤ ਬਨਾਵੈ।","roman":"Mai kabhoo nahee jaau tahaa tuh see kahi kotik baat banaavai |","meaning_en":"I will never go there, even if ones like you make up ten million stories;","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਕੀ ਕਉਨ ਗਨੈ ਗਨਤੀ ਬਲਿ ਆਪਨ ਕਾਨ ਜੂ ਸੀਸ ਝੁਕਾਵੈ। ੭੨੦।","roman":"Aur kee kaun ganai gantee bali aapan kaan joo sees jhukaavai | 720 |","meaning_en":"who counts anyone else, dear? Even if Kanh himself bows his head.'","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਪ੍ਰਤਿਉਤਰ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਤਿਉਤਰ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Pratiutar baach","meaning_en":"Reply:","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[721],"number_text":"੭੨੧।","page":450,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋ ਇਨ ਐਸੀ ਕਹੀ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਤਬ ਹੀ ਉਹ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਯੌ ਕਹਿਯੌ ਹੋ ਰੀ।","roman":"Jo in aisee kahee bateeyaa tab hee uh gvaarni yau kahiyau ho ree |","meaning_en":"When she said such words, that gopi then said thus: 'Oh!","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਉ ਹਮ ਬਾਤ ਕਹੀ ਚਲੀਯੈ ਤੂ ਕਹੈ ਹਮ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਸੋ ਪ੍ਰੀਤ ਹੀ ਛੋਰੀ।","roman":"Jau ham baat kahee chaleeyai too kahai ham syaam so preet hee chhoree |","meaning_en":"When I said, \"Come,\" you say, \"I have given up my love for Shyam.\"","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਸੋ ਮਾਈ ਕਹਾ ਕਹੀਯੈ ਇਹ ਸਾਥ ਕਰੇ ਹਿਤਵਾ ਬਰ ਜੋਰੀ।","roman":"Syaam so maaee kahaa kaheeyai ih saath kare hitvaa bar joree |","meaning_en":"Mother, what can one say to Shyam? He has joined in love with this one by force;","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਰ ਜੋਰੀ: read as 'by force' or 'perfectly matched'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭੇਜਤ ਹੈ ਹਮ ਕੋ ਇਹ ਪੈ ਇਹ ਸੀ ਤਿਹ ਕੇ ਪਹਿ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਥੋਰੀ। ੭੨੧।","roman":"Bhejat hai ham ko ih pai ih see tih ke pahi gvaarni thoree | 721 |","meaning_en":"he sends me to her, yet he has no lack of gopis like her.'","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[722],"number_text":"੭੨੨।","page":450,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭੇਜਤ ਹੈ ਇਹ ਪੈ ਹਮ ਕੋ ਇਹ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਰੂਪ ਕੋ ਮਾਨ ਕਰੈ।","roman":"Bhejat hai ih pai ham ko ih gvaarni roop ko maan karai |","meaning_en":"'He sends me to this one, and this gopi is proud of her beauty;","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਇਹ ਜਾਨਤ ਵੈ ਘਟ ਹੈ ਹਮ ਤੇ ਤਿਹ ਤੇ ਹਠ ਬਾਧਿ ਰਹੀ ਨ ਟਰੈ।","roman":"Ih jaanat vai ghat hai ham te tih te hath baadhi rahee na tarai |","meaning_en":"she thinks the others are less than her, so she holds fast to her stubbornness and will not budge.'","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਪਿਖੋ ਇਹ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਕੀ ਮਤਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕੇ ਕੋਪ ਤੇ ਪੈ ਨ ਡਰੈ।","roman":"Kabi syaam pikho ih gvaarni kee mati syaam ke kop te pai na darai |","meaning_en":"The poet Shyam says, see this gopi's mind: she does not fear Shyam's anger;","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਹ ਸੋ ਬਲਿ ਜਾਉ ਕਹਾ ਕਹੀਯੈ ਤਿਹ ਲ੍ਯਾਵਹੁ ਯੋ ਮੁਖ ਤੇ ਉਚਰੈ। ੭੨੨।","roman":"Tih so bali jaau kahaa kaheeyai tih lyaavhu yo mukh te uchrai | 722 |","meaning_en":"'I am devoted to him; what can be said? He says with his own mouth, \"Bring her.\"'","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[723],"number_text":"੭੨੩।","page":450,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਰੈ ਸਖੀ ਅਉਰ ਸੋ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਤਬੈ ਇਹ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਭੂਲ ਪਛਾਨੈ।","roman":"Syaam karai sakhee aur so preeti tabai ih gvaarni bhool pachhaanai |","meaning_en":"'Friend, when Shyam makes love with another, then this gopi will know her mistake;","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਵਾ ਕੇ ਕੀਏ ਬਿਨੁ ਰੀ ਸਜਨੀ ਸੁ ਰਹੀ ਕਹਿ ਕੈ ਸੁ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਨਹੀ ਮਾਨੈ।","roman":"Vaa ke kee'e binu ree sajnee su rahee kahi kai su kahiyo nahee maanai |","meaning_en":"until that happens, friend, she does not heed what is said to her, however much one says;","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯਾ ਕੋ ਬਿਸਾਰ ਡਰੈ ਮਨ ਤੇ ਤਬ ਹੀ ਇਹ ਮਾਨਹਿ ਕੋ ਫਲੁ ਜਾਨੈ।","roman":"Yaa ko bisaar darai man te tab hee ih maanhi ko phalu jaanai |","meaning_en":"when he puts her out of his mind, then she will know the fruit of this pique;","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅੰਤ ਖਿਸਾਇ ਘਨੀ ਅਕੁਲਾਇ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਤਬ ਹੀ ਇਹ ਮਾਨੈ ਤੁ ਮਾਨੈ।੭੨੩।","roman":"Ant khisaai ghanee akulaai kahiyo tab hee ih maanai tu maanai | 723 |","meaning_en":"in the end, much ashamed and distressed, she will agree then, if she agrees at all.'","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Line read loosely; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[724],"number_text":"੭੨੪।","page":450,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੋ ਸੁਨ ਕੈ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਤਿਹ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਕੋ ਇਮ ਉਤਰ ਦੀਨੋ।","roman":"Yo sun kai brikhbhaan sutaa tih gvaarni ko im utar deeno |","meaning_en":"Hearing this, Brikhbhan's daughter gave that gopi this answer:","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰੀਤ ਕਰੀ ਹਰਿ ਚੰਦ੍ਰਭਗਾ ਸੰਗ ਤਉ ਹਮ ਹੂੰ ਅਸ ਮਾਨ ਸੁ ਕੀਨੋ।","roman":"Preet karee hari chandrabhgaa sang tau ham hoon as maan su keeno |","meaning_en":"'Krishna made love with Chandrabhaga, so I too took such pique;","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਉ ਸਜਨੀ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਰੂਠ ਰਹੀ ਅਤਿ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਬਢਿਯੋ ਹਮਰੇ ਜਬ ਜੀਨੋ।","roman":"Tau sajnee kahiyo rooth rahee ati krodh badhiyo hamre jab jeeno |","meaning_en":"that is why, friend, I stay sulking; great anger grew in my heart when I knew it;","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜੀਨੋ: read as 'knew'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੇਰੇ ਕਹੇ ਬਿਨੁ ਰੀ ਹਰਿ ਆਗੇ ਹੂੰ ਮੋ ਹੂ ਸੋ ਨੇਹੁ ਬਿਦਾ ਕਰ ਦੀਨੋ। ੭੨੪।","roman":"Tere kahe binu ree hari aage hoon mo hoo so nehu bidaa kar deeno | 724 |","meaning_en":"even before your words, Krishna had already sent away his love for me.'","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[725],"number_text":"੭੨੫।","page":450,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੋ ਕਹਿ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਸੋ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਫਿਰਿ ਐਸੇ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਹੈ।","roman":"Yo kahi gvaarni so bateeyaa kabi syaam kahai phiri aise kahiyo hai |","meaning_en":"Having said these words to the gopi, says the poet Shyam, she spoke again thus:","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਹਿ ਰੀ ਕਾਹੇ ਕੋ ਬੈਠੀ ਹੈ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਤੇਰੋ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਮੈ ਸਹਿਯੋ ਹੈ।","roman":"Jaahi ree kaahe ko baithee hai gvaarni tero kahiyo ati hee mai sahiyo hai |","meaning_en":"'Go, why do you sit here, gopi? I have borne a great deal of your talk;","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਤ ਕਹੀ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਰਸ ਕੀ ਤੁਹਿ ਤਾ ਕੋ ਨ ਸੋ ਸਖੀ ਚਿਤ ਚਹਿਯੋ ਹੈ।","roman":"Baat kahee ati hee ras kee tuhi taa ko na so sakhee chit chahiyo hai |","meaning_en":"you have spoken words full of love, but my heart, friend, does not want him;","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਤੇ ਹਉ ਨ ਚਲੋ ਸਜਨੀ ਹਮ ਸੋ ਹਰਿ ਸੋ ਰਸ ਕਉਨ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਹੈ। ੭੨੫।","roman":"Taahee te hau na chalo sajnee ham so hari so ras kaun rahiyo hai | 725 |","meaning_en":"so I will not go, friend; what love is left between Krishna and me?'","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[726],"number_text":"੭੨੬।","page":450,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਸੁਨਿ ਉਤਰ ਦੇਤ ਭਈ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਹਰਿ ਕੇ ਹਿਤ ਕੇਰੋ।","roman":"Yau suni utar det bhaee kabi syaam kahai hari ke hit kero |","meaning_en":"Hearing this, she gave an answer, says the poet Shyam, for Krishna's love:","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਕੇ ਭੇਜੇ ਤੇ ਯਾ ਪਹਿ ਆਇਕੈ ਕੈ ਕੈ ਮਨਾਵਨ ਕੋ ਅਤਿ ਝੇਰੋ।","roman":"Kaanh ke bheje te yaa pahi aaikai kai kai manaavan ko ati jhero |","meaning_en":"having come here sent by Kanh, and having pleaded so many times to win her over —","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਝੇਰੋ: read as 'pleading, trouble'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਚਕੋਰ ਮਨੋ ਤ੍ਰਨ ਜੋ ਸੁਨ ਰੀ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਕਹੈ ਮਨ ਮੇਰੋ।","roman":"Syaam chakor mano tran jo sun ree ih bhaati kahai man mero |","meaning_en":"'Shyam is like a chakor bird, listen; this is what my heart says:","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"The chakor is said to gaze at the moon."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਨਿਹਾਰਿ ਨਿਹਾਰਿ ਸੁਨੋ ਸਸਿ ਸੋ ਮੁਖ ਦੇਖਤ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਹੈ ਰੀ ਤੇਰੋ। ੭੨੬।","roman":"Taahee nihaari nihaari suno sasi so mukh dekhat hvai hai ree tero | 726 |","meaning_en":"gazing and gazing, listen, he will be looking at your moon-like face.'","page":450,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Raadhe baach","meaning_en":"Radha said:","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[727],"number_text":"੭੨੭।","page":451,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਖਤ ਹੈ ਤੁ ਕਹਾ ਭਯੋ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਮੈ ਨ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਤਿਹ ਕੇ ਪਹਿ ਜੈਹੋ।","roman":"Dekhat hai tu kahaa bhayo gvaarni mai na kahiyo tih ke pahi jaiho |","meaning_en":"'What if he is looking, gopi? I have said I will not go to him;","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਹੇ ਕੇ ਕਾਜ ਉਰਾਹਨ ਰੀ ਸਹਿ ਹੋ ਅਪਨੋ ਪਤਿ ਦੇਖਿ ਅਘੈ ਹੋ।","roman":"Kaahe ke kaaj uraahan ree sahi ho apno pati dekhi aghai ho |","meaning_en":"why should I bear reproaches? I will be content just seeing my lord from afar;","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਘੈ ਹੋ: read as 'be satisfied'; line uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਰਚੇ ਸੰਗਿ ਅਉਰ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਤਿਹ ਕੇ ਪਹਿ ਜਾਇ ਕਹਾ ਜਸ ਪੈਹੋ।","roman":"Syaam rache sangi aur treeyaa tih ke pahi jaai kahaa jas paiho |","meaning_en":"Shyam is taken up with another woman; what credit will I gain by going to him?","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਤੇ ਪਧਾਰਹੁ ਰੀ ਸਜਨੀ ਹਰਿ ਕੌ ਨਹਿ ਜੀਵਤ ਰੂਪ ਦਿਖੈ ਹੋ। ੭੨੭।","roman":"Taa te padhaarhu ree sajnee hari kau nahi jeevat roop dikhai ho | 727 |","meaning_en":"So go away, friend; as long as I live I will not show Krishna my face.'","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"section_heading","name":"ਅਥ ਮੈਨ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਕ੍ਰਿਸਨ ਜੀ ਪਾਸ ਫਿਰ ਆਈ","gurmukhi":"ਅਥ ਮੈਨ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਕ੍ਰਿਸਨ ਜੀ ਪਾਸ ਫਿਰ ਆਈ","roman":"Ath main prabhaa krisan jee paas phir aaee","meaning_en":"Now Mainprabha came back to Krishna.","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਦੂਤੀ ਬਾਚ ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਸੋ","gurmukhi":"ਦੂਤੀ ਬਾਚ ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਸੋ","roman":"Dootee baach kaanh joo so","meaning_en":"The messenger said to Kanh:","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[728],"number_text":"੭੨੮।","page":451,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਜਬ ਤਾਹਿ ਸੁਨੀ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਉਠ ਕੈ ਸੋਊ ਨੰਦ ਲਲਾ ਪਹਿ ਆਈ।","roman":"Yau jab taahi sunee bateeyaa uth kai so'oo nand lalaa pahi aaee |","meaning_en":"When she heard these words, she rose and came to Nand's darling;","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਇ ਕੈ ਐਸੇ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਹਰਿ ਪੈ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਨਹਿ ਮਾਨਤ ਮੂੜ ਮਨਾਈ।","roman":"Aai kai aise kahiyo hari pai hari joo nahi maanat moor manaaee |","meaning_en":"coming, she said thus to Krishna: 'Krishna, the foolish one will not be won over;","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੈ ਤਜਿ ਵਾਹਿ ਰਚੌ ਇਨ ਸੋ ਨਹੀ ਆਪ ਹੂੰ ਜਾਇ ਕੈ ਲਿਆਉ ਮਨਾਈ।","roman":"Kai taji vaahi rachau in so nahee aap hoon jaai kai liaau manaaee |","meaning_en":"either leave her and give yourself to these others, or else go yourself and win her over and bring her.'","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਸੁਨਿ ਬਾਤ ਚਲਿਯੋ ਤਹ ਕੋ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਹਰਿ ਆਪ ਹੀ ਧਾਈ। ੭੨੮।","roman":"Yau suni baat chaliyo tah ko kabi syaam kahai hari aap hee dhaaee | 728 |","meaning_en":"Hearing this, says the poet Shyam, Krishna himself set off and hurried there.","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[729],"number_text":"੭੨੯।","page":451,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਨ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਿਨਿ ਕੋਊ ਪਠੀ ਚਲਿ ਕੈ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਤਬ ਆਪ ਹੀ ਆਯੋ।","roman":"Aur na gvaarini ko'oo pathee chali kai hari joo tab aap hee aayo |","meaning_en":"He sent no other gopi; Krishna then came there himself;","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਕੋ ਰੂਪ ਨਿਹਾਰਤ ਹੀ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਸੁਖ ਪਾਯੋ।","roman":"Taahee ko roop nihaarat hee brikhbhaan sutaa man mai sukh paayo |","meaning_en":"as soon as she beheld his form, Brikhbhan's daughter felt joy in her heart;","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਇ ਘਨੋ ਸੁਖ ਪੈ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਅਤਿ ਊਪਰਿ ਮਾਨ ਸੋ ਬੋਲ ਸੁਨਾਯੋ।","roman":"Paai ghano sukh pai man mai ati oopri maan so bol sunaayo |","meaning_en":"though she felt great joy within, outwardly she spoke with pique:","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚੰਦ੍ਰਭਗਾ ਹੂੰ ਸੋ ਕੇਲ ਕਰੋ ਇਹ ਠਉਰ ਕਹਾ ਤਜਿ ਲਾਜਹਿ ਆਯੋ। ੭੨੯।","roman":"Chandrabhgaa hoon so kel karo ih thaur kahaa taji laajhi aayo | 729 |","meaning_en":"'Make love with Chandrabhaga; why have you come to this place, leaving shame behind?'","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਸੋ","gurmukhi":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਸੋ","roman":"Raadhe baach kaanh joo so","meaning_en":"Radha said to Kanh:","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[730],"number_text":"੭੩੦।","page":451,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਸਹਿ ਕਿਉ ਤਜਿ ਚੰਦ੍ਰਭਗਾ ਚਲਿ ਕੈ ਹਮਰੇ ਪਹਿ ਕਿਉ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਆਯੋ।","roman":"Raashi kiu taji chandrabhgaa chali kai hamre pahi kiu kahiyo aayo |","meaning_en":"'Why have you left the Ras and Chandrabhaga and come to me? Tell me, why have you come?","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਉ ਇਹ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਕੀ ਸਿਖ ਮਾਨ ਕੈ ਆਪਨ ਹੀ ਉਠ ਕੈ ਸਖੀ ਧਾਯੋ।","roman":"Kiu ih gvaarni kee sikh maan kai aapan hee uth kai sakhee dhaayo |","meaning_en":"Why, heeding this gopi's advice, did you rise and run here yourself, friend?","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਨਤ ਥੀ ਕਿ ਬਡੋ ਠਗੁ ਹੈ ਇਹ ਬਾਤਨ ਤੇ ਅਬ ਹੀ ਲਖਿ ਪਾਯੋ।","roman":"Jaanat thee ki bado thagu hai ih baatan te ab hee lakhi paayo |","meaning_en":"I knew you were a great cheat; from these words I have seen it now;","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਉ ਹਮਰੇ ਪਹਿ ਆਏ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਹਮ ਤੋ ਤੁਮ ਕੋ ਨਹੀ ਬੋਲਿ ਪਠਾਯੋ। ੭੩੦।","roman":"Kiu hamre pahi aae kahiyo ham to tum ko nahee boli pathaayo | 730 |","meaning_en":"why have you come to me? I certainly did not send for you.'","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਬਾਚ ਰਾਧੇ ਸੋ","gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਬਾਚ ਰਾਧੇ ਸੋ","roman":"Kaanh joo baach raadhe so","meaning_en":"Kanh said to Radha:","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[731],"number_text":"੭੩੧।","page":451,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਸੁਨਿ ਉਤਰ ਦੇਤ ਭਯੋ ਨਹਿ ਰੀ ਤੁਹਿ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਬੋਲ ਪਠਾਯੋ।","roman":"Yau suni utar det bhayo nahi ree tuhi gvaarni bol pathaayo |","meaning_en":"Hearing this, he answered: 'No, the gopi did not send for me;","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨੈਨਨ ਕੇ ਕਰਿ ਭਾਵ ਘਨੇ ਸਰ ਸੋ ਹਮਰੋ ਮਨੂਆ ਮ੍ਰਿਗ ਘਾਯੋ।","roman":"Nainan ke kari bhaav ghane sar so hamro manooaa mrig ghaayo |","meaning_en":"with the many gestures of your eyes, as with arrows, you have wounded the deer of my heart;","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਬਿਰਹਾਗਨਿ ਸੋ ਸੁਨੀਯੈ ਬਲਿ ਅੰਗ ਜਰਿਯੋ ਸੁ ਗਯੋ ਨ ਬਚਾਯੋ।","roman":"Taa birhaagni so suneeyai bali ang jariyo su gayo na bachaayo |","meaning_en":"listen, dear: in that fire of separation my limbs were burning and could not be saved;","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੇਰੇ ਬੁਲਾਯੋ ਨ ਆਯੋ ਹੋ ਰੀ ਤਿਹ ਠਉਰ ਜਰੇ ਕਹੁ ਸੇਕਿਨਿ ਆਯੋ। ੭੩੧।","roman":"Tere bulaayo na aayo ho ree tih thaur jare kahu sekini aayo | 731 |","meaning_en":"I have not come because you called me; I came to that place, burning, to warm myself (at your fire).'","page":451,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੇਕਿਨਿ: read as 'to warm/soothe oneself'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਸੋ","gurmukhi":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਸੋ","roman":"Raadhe baach kaanh so","meaning_en":"Radha said to Kanh:","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[732],"number_text":"੭੩੨।","page":452,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਗ ਫਿਰੀ ਤੁਮਰੇ ਹਰਿ ਖੇਲਤ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੇ ਕਬਿ ਆਨੰਦ ਭੀਨੀ।","roman":"Sang phiree tumre hari khelat syaam kahe kabi aanand bheenee |","meaning_en":"'I wandered with you, Krishna, playing, says the poet Shyam, steeped in joy;","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲੋਗਨ ਕੋ ਉਪਹਾਸ ਸਹਿਯੋ ਤੁਹਿ ਮੂਰਤਿ ਚੀਨ ਕੈ ਅਉਰ ਨ ਚੀਨੀ।","roman":"Logan ko uphaas sahiyo tuhi moorti cheen kai aur na cheenee |","meaning_en":"I bore people's mockery; I recognised your form and recognised no other;","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੇਤ ਕਰਿਯੋ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਤੁਮ ਸੋ ਤੁਮ ਹੂੰ ਤਜਿ ਹੇਤ ਦਸਾ ਇਹ ਕੀਨੀ।","roman":"Het kariyo ati hee tum so tum hoon taji het dasaa ih keenee |","meaning_en":"I loved you very greatly, and you abandoned that love and brought me to this state;","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਕਰੀ ਸੰਗ ਅਉਰ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਕਹਿ ਸਾਸ ਲਯੋ ਅਖੀਯਾ ਭਰ ਲੀਨੀ। ੭੩੨।","roman":"Preeti karee sang aur treeyaa kahi saas layo akheeyaa bhar leenee | 732 |","meaning_en":"you made love with another woman.' Saying this, she sighed and her eyes filled with tears.","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Kaanh joo baach","meaning_en":"Kanh said:","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[733],"number_text":"੭੩੩।","page":452,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੇਰੋ ਘਨੋ ਹਿਤ ਹੈ ਤੁਮ ਸੋ ਸਖੀ ਅਉਰ ਕਿਸੀ ਨਹਿ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਮਾਹੀ।","roman":"Mero ghano hit hai tum so sakhee aur kisee nahi gvaarni maahee |","meaning_en":"'My love is great for you, friend, and for no other among the gopis;","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੇਰੇ ਖਰੇ ਤੁਹਿ ਦੇਖਤ ਹੋ ਬਿਨ ਤ੍ਵੈ ਤੁਹਿ ਮੂਰਤਿ ਕੀ ਪਰਛਾਹੀ।","roman":"Tere khare tuhi dekhat ho bin tvai tuhi moorti kee parchhaahee |","meaning_en":"when you stand before me I see you; without you I see the shadow of your form.'","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਕਹਿ ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਗਹੀ ਬਹੀਯਾ ਚਲੀਯੈ ਹਮ ਸੋ ਬਨ ਮੈ ਸੁਖ ਪਾਹੀ।","roman":"Yau kahi kaanh gahee baheeyaa chaleeyai ham so ban mai sukh paahee |","meaning_en":"Saying this, Kanh took her by the arm: 'Come with me, let us find joy in the forest;","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹ ਹਾ ਚਲੁ ਮੇਰੀ ਸਹੁੰ ਮੇਰੀ ਸਹੁੰ ਮੇਰੀ ਸਹੁੰ ਤੇਰੀ ਸਹੁੰ ਤੇਰੀ ਸਹੁੰ ਨਾਹੀ ਜੂ ਨਾਹੀ। ੭੩੩।","roman":"Ha haa chalu meree sahun meree sahun meree sahun teree sahun teree sahun naahee joo naahee | 733 |","meaning_en":"oh, come, I swear by myself, I swear by myself, I swear by you, I swear by you.' 'No, sir, no.'","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Repeated oaths ਸਹੁੰ; the final 'ਨਾਹੀ ਜੂ ਨਾਹੀ' read as Radha's refusal; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[734],"number_text":"੭੩੪।","page":452,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਕਹਿ ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਗਹੀ ਬਿਹੀਯਾ ਤਿਹੂ ਲੋਗਨ ਕੋ ਭੁਗੀਯਾ ਰਸ ਜੋ ਹੈ।","roman":"Yau kahi kaanh gahee biheeyaa tihoo logan ko bhugeeyaa ras jo hai |","meaning_en":"Saying this, Kanh took her by the arm, he who is the enjoyer of delight of the three worlds,","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੇਹਰਿ ਸੀ ਜਿਹ ਕੀ ਕਟਿ ਹੈ ਜਿਹ ਆਨਨ ਪੈ ਸਸਿ ਕੋਟਿਕ ਕੋ ਹੈ।","roman":"Kehri see jih kee kati hai jih aanan pai sasi kotik ko hai |","meaning_en":"whose waist is like a lion's, and whose face outshines ten million moons;","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਐਸੋ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਚਲੀਯੈ ਹਮਰੇ ਸੰਗਿ ਜੋ ਸਭ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਕੋ ਮਨ ਮੋਹੈ।","roman":"Aiso kahiyo chaleeyai hamre sangi jo sabh gvaarni ko man mohai |","meaning_en":"he who charms the hearts of all the gopis said thus: 'Come with me.'","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਕਹਿ ਕਾਹੇ ਕਰੋ ਬਿਨਤੀ ਸੁਨ ਕੈ ਤੁਹਿ ਲਾਲ ਹੀਐ ਮਧਿ ਜੋ ਹੈ। ੭੩੪।","roman":"Yau kahi kaahe karo bintee sun kai tuhi laal heeai madhi jo hai | 734 |","meaning_en":"'Why do you plead thus? Listen: the darling who is in your heart (is here).'","page":452,"flags":[{"code":"ੈੈ","reason":"same sign typed twice; written once (prints as one)"}],"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Line read loosely; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[735],"number_text":"੭੩੫।","page":452,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਹੇ ਉਰਾਹਨ ਦੇਤ ਸਖੀ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਪ੍ਰੀਤ ਘਨੀ ਹਮਰੀ ਸੰਗ ਤੇਰੇ।","roman":"Kaahe uraahan det sakhee kahiyo preet ghanee hamree sang tere |","meaning_en":"'Why do you reproach me, friend?' he said; 'my love for you is great;","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਾਹਕ ਤੂੰ ਭਰਮੀ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਕਛੁ ਬਾਤ ਨ ਚੰਦ੍ਰਭਗਾ ਮਨਿ ਮੇਰੇ।","roman":"Naahak toon bharmee man mai kachhu baat na chandrabhgaa mani mere |","meaning_en":"you are deluded in your mind for nothing; Chandrabhaga is nothing to my heart;","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਤੇ ਉਠੋ ਤਜਿ ਮਾਨ ਸਭੈ ਚਲਿ ਖੇਲਹਿੰ ਪੈ ਜਮੁਨਾ ਤਟਿ ਕੇਰੇ।","roman":"Taa te utho taji maan sabhai chali khelhin pai jamunaa tati kere |","meaning_en":"so rise, give up all pique, and come; let us play on the bank of the Yamuna.'","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਨਤ ਹੈ ਨਹਿ ਬਾਤ ਹਠੀ ਬਿਰਹਾਤੁਰ ਹੈ ਬਿਰਹੀ ਜਨ ਟੇਰੇ। ੭੩੫।","roman":"Maanat hai nahi baat hathee birhaatur hai birhee jan tere | 735 |","meaning_en":"The stubborn one would not heed his words; the one tormented by separation calls out to his beloved.","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Line read loosely; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[736],"number_text":"੭੩੬।","page":452,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਯਾਗ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਅਬ ਮਾਨ ਸਖੀ ਹਮ ਹੂੰ ਤੁਮ ਹੂੰ ਬਨ ਬੀਚ ਪਧਾਰੈ।","roman":"Tyaag kahiyo ab maan sakhee ham hoon tum hoon ban beech padhaarai |","meaning_en":"'Give up your pique now, friend,' he said; 'let you and me go into the forest;","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਾਹਕ ਹੀ ਤੂ ਰਿਸੀ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਨਹੀ ਆਨ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਮਨ ਬਾਤ ਹਮਾਰੈ।","roman":"Naahak hee too risee man mai nahee aan treeyaa man baat hamaarai |","meaning_en":"you are angry in your heart for nothing; no other woman is in my thoughts;","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਤੇ ਅਸੋਕ ਕੇ ਸਾਥ ਸੁਨੋ ਬਲਿ ਤੀਰ ਨਦੀ ਸਭ ਸੋਕਹਿ ਡਾਰੈ।","roman":"Taa te asok ke saath suno bali teer nadee sabh sokhi daarai |","meaning_en":"so listen, dear: by the asoka tree, on the river bank, let us cast away all sorrow;","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਸੋਕ: the asoka tree, also 'free of sorrow'; wordplay."},{"gurmukhi":"ਯਾ ਤੇ ਨ ਅਉਰ ਭਲੀ ਕਛੁ ਹੈ ਮਿਲਿ ਕੈ ਹਮ ਮੈਨ ਕੋ ਮਾਨ ਨਿਵਾਰੈ। ੭੩੬।","roman":"Yaa te na aur bhalee kachhu hai mili kai ham main ko maan nivaarai | 736 |","meaning_en":"there is nothing better than this: together let us humble the pride of Kamdev.'","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[737],"number_text":"੭੩੭।","page":452,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਰਸਾਤਰ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਢਿਗ ਬਾਤ ਉਚਾਰੀ।","roman":"Kaanh rasaatar hvai ati hee brikhbhaan sutaa dhig baat uchaaree |","meaning_en":"Kanh, deeply eager in love, spoke these words close to Brikhbhan's daughter;","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰਸਾਤਰ: read as 'eager in love'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹਿ ਮਨੀ ਹਰਿ ਬਾਤ ਸੋਊ ਤਿਨ ਮਾਨ ਕੀ ਬਾਤ ਬਿਦਾ ਕਰਿ ਡਾਰੀ।","roman":"Taahi manee hari baat so'oo tin maan kee baat bidaa kari daaree |","meaning_en":"she accepted Krishna's word and sent away all thought of pique;","page":452,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਾਥਹਿ ਸੋ ਬਹੀਆ ਗਹਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਸੁ ਐਸੇ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਅਬ ਖੇਲਹਿ ਯਾਰੀ।","roman":"Haathhi so baheeaa gahi syaam su aise kahiyo ab khelhi yaaree |","meaning_en":"taking her arm in his hand, Shyam said thus: 'Now let us play, beloved;'","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਤਬ ਰਾਧਕਾ ਸੋ ਹਮਰੇ ਸੰਗ ਕੇਲ ਕਰੋ ਮੋਰੀ ਪਿਆਰੀ। ੭੩੭।","roman":"Kaanh kahiyo tab raadhkaa so hamre sang kel karo moree piaaree | 737 |","meaning_en":"then Kanh said to Radhika, 'Play with me, my darling.'","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਸੋ","gurmukhi":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਸੋ","roman":"Raadhe baach kaanh so","meaning_en":"Radha said to Kanh:","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[738],"number_text":"੭੩੮।","page":453,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਸੁਨਿ ਕੈ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਨੰਦ ਲਾਲ ਲਲਾ ਕਹੁ ਉਤਰ ਦੀਨੋ।","roman":"Yau suni kai brikhbhaan sutaa nand laal lalaa kahu utar deeno |","meaning_en":"Hearing this, Brikhbhan's daughter answered Nand's darling:","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਸੋ ਬਾਤ ਕਰੋ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਜਿਹ ਕੇ ਸੰਗ ਨੇਹੁ ਘਨੋ ਤੁਮ ਕੀਨੋ।","roman":"Taahee so baat karo hari joo jih ke sang nehu ghano tum keeno |","meaning_en":"'Krishna, talk with the one with whom you have made such great love;","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਹੇ ਕਉ ਮੋਰੀ ਗਹੀ ਬਹੀਆ ਸੁ ਦੁਖਾਵਤ ਕਾਹੇ ਕਉ ਹੋ ਮੁਹਿ ਜੀ ਨੋ।","roman":"Kaahe kau moree gahee baheeaa su dukhaavat kaahe kau ho muhi jee no |","meaning_en":"why have you taken my arm? Why do you pain my heart?'","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਕਹਿ ਬਾਤ ਭਰੀ ਅਖੀਆ ਕਰਿ ਕੈ ਦੁਖ ਸਾਸ ਉਸਾਸ ਸੁ ਲੀਨੋ। ੭੩੮।","roman":"Yau kahi baat bharee akheeaa kari kai dukh saas usaas su leeno | 738 |","meaning_en":"Saying these words, her eyes filled, and in sorrow she sighed deeply.","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[739],"number_text":"੭੩੯।","page":453,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕੇਲ ਕਰੋ ਉਠਿ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਸੋ ਜਿਨਿ ਸੰਗ ਰਚਿਯੋ ਮਨ ਹੈ ਸੁ ਤੁਮਾਰੋ।","roman":"Kel karo uthi gvaarni so jini sang rachiyo man hai su tumaaro |","meaning_en":"'Rise and play with the gopi with whom your heart has become taken up.'","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਵਾਸਨ ਲੈ ਅਖੀਆ ਭਰ ਕੈ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਉਚਾਰੋ।","roman":"Svaasan lai akheeaa bhar kai brikhbhaan sutaa ih bhaati uchaaro |","meaning_en":"Sighing, with eyes filled with tears, Brikhbhan's daughter spoke in this way:","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਗ ਚਲੋ ਨਹਿ ਹਉ ਤੁਮਰੇ ਕਰਿ ਆਯੁਧ ਲੈ ਕਹਿਓ ਕਿਉ ਨਹੀ ਮਾਰੋ।","roman":"Sang chalo nahi hau tumre kari aayudh lai kahio kiu nahee maaro |","meaning_en":"'I will not go with you; take a weapon in your hand,' she said, 'why do you not kill me?","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਚ ਕਹੋ ਤੁਮ ਸੋ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਤਜਿ ਕੈ ਹਮ ਕੋ ਜਦੁਬੀਰ ਪਧਾਰੋ। ੭੩੯।","roman":"Saach kaho tum so bateeyaa taji kai ham ko jadubeer padhaaro | 739 |","meaning_en":"I tell you the truth: leave me, Yadav hero, and go away.'","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਬਾਚ ਰਾਧੇ ਸੋ","gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਬਾਚ ਰਾਧੇ ਸੋ","roman":"Kaanh joo baach raadhe so","meaning_en":"Kanh said to Radha:","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[740],"number_text":"੭੪੦।","page":453,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਗ ਚਲੋ ਹਮਰੇ ਉਠ ਕੈ ਸਖੀ ਮਾਨ ਕਛੁ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਨਹੀ ਆਨੋ।","roman":"Sang chalo hamre uth kai sakhee maan kachhu man mai nahee aano |","meaning_en":"'Rise and come with me, friend; hold no pique in your heart;","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਇ ਹੋ ਹਉ ਤਜਿ ਸੰਕਿ ਨਿਸੰਕ ਕਛੂ ਤਿਹ ਤੇ ਰਸ ਰੀਤਿ ਪਛਾਨੋ।","roman":"Aai ho hau taji sanki nisank kachhoo tih te ras reeti pachhaano |","meaning_en":"I have come, leaving all doubt, without fear; so recognise from this the ways of love;","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਿਤ੍ਰ ਕੇ ਬੇਚੇ ਕਿਧੌ ਬਿਕੀਯੈ ਇਹ ਸ੍ਰਉਨ ਸੁਨੋ ਸਖੀ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਕਹਾਨੋ।","roman":"Mitr ke beche kidhau bikeeyai ih sraun suno sakhee preeti kahaano |","meaning_en":"when a friend sells us, we are sold; hear with your ears, friend, this tale of love;","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Line read loosely; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਤੇ ਹਉ ਤੇਰੀ ਕਰੋ ਬਿਨਤੀ ਕਹਿਬੋ ਮੁਹਿ ਮਾਨਿ ਸਖੀ ਅਬ ਮਾਨੋ। ੭੪੦।","roman":"Taa te hau teree karo bintee kahibo muhi maani sakhee ab maano | 740 |","meaning_en":"so I make my plea to you: heed what I say, friend, and agree now.'","page":453,"flags":[{"code":"0x66","reason":"sihari typed before the previous letter's ੁ; attached to the next consonant"}],"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਰਾਧੇ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Raadhe baach","meaning_en":"Radha said:","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[741],"number_text":"੭੪੧।","page":453,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਸੁਨਿ ਕੈ ਹਰਿ ਕੀ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਹਰਿ ਕੋ ਤਿਨ ਯਾ ਬਿਧਿ ਉਤਰ ਦੀਨੋ।","roman":"Yau suni kai hari kee bateeyaa hari ko tin yaa bidhi utar deeno |","meaning_en":"Hearing these words of Krishna, she answered Krishna in this way:","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਰਹੀ ਹਮ ਸੋ ਤੁਮਰੀ ਕਹਾ ਯੌ ਕਹਿ ਕੈ ਦ੍ਰਿਗਿ ਬਾਰਿ ਭਰੀਨੋ।","roman":"Preeti rahee ham so tumree kahaa yau kahi kai drigi baari bhareeno |","meaning_en":"'Where is your love for me now?' Saying this, her eyes filled with tears;","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਕਰੀ ਸੰਗ ਚੰਦ੍ਰਭਗਾ ਅਤਿ ਕੋਪ ਬਢਿਯੋ ਤਿਹ ਤੇ ਮੁਹਿ ਜੀ ਨੋ।","roman":"Preeti karee sang chandrabhgaa ati kop badhiyo tih te muhi jee no |","meaning_en":"'you made love with Chandrabhaga; that is why great anger has risen in my heart.'","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਕਹਿ ਕੈ ਭਰਿ ਸ੍ਵਾਸ ਲਯੌ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਕਪਟੀਨੋ। ੭੪੧।","roman":"Yau kahi kai bhari svaas layau kabi syaam kahai ati hee kapteeno | 741 |","meaning_en":"Saying this, she heaved a sigh, says the poet Shyam, full of artful guile.","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਪਟੀਨੋ: 'wily, feigning'."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[742],"number_text":"੭੪੨।","page":453,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਭਰੀ ਫਿਰਿ ਬੋਲਿ ਉਠੀ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨੁ ਸੁਤਾ ਮੁਖ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਸਿਉ।","roman":"Krodh bharee phiri boli uthee brikhbhaanu sutaa mukh sundar siu |","meaning_en":"Filled with anger, Brikhbhan's daughter spoke again from her lovely mouth:","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੁਮ ਸੋ ਹਮ ਸੋ ਰਸ ਕਉਨ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਬਿਧਿ ਕੋ ਪਹਿ ਜਿਉ।","roman":"Tum so ham so ras kaun rahiyo kabi syaam kahai bidhi ko pahi jiu |","meaning_en":"'What love is left between you and me?' says the poet Shyam, as if by fate's decree;","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਿਧਿ ਕੋ ਪਹਿ ਜਿਉ: read loosely; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਰਿ ਯੌ ਕਹੀ ਮੋ ਹਿਤ ਹੈ ਤੁਹਿ ਸੋ ਉਨਿ ਕੋਪਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਹਮ ਸੋ ਕਹੁ ਕਿਉ।","roman":"Hari yau kahee mo hit hai tuhi so uni kopi kahiyo ham so kahu kiu |","meaning_en":"Krishna said thus: 'My love is for you.' She said in anger, 'Why tell me so?'","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੁਮਰੇ ਸੰਗਿ ਕੇਲ ਕਰੇ ਬਨ ਮੈ ਸੁਨੀਯੈ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਹਮਰੀ ਬਲਿ ਇਉ। ੭੪੨।","roman":"Tumre sangi kel kare ban mai suneeyai bateeyaa hamree bali iu | 742 |","meaning_en":"'I would play with you in the forest; listen to my words, dear, thus.'","page":453,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Line read as Krishna's; uncertain."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਬਾਚ ਰਾਧੇ ਸੋ","gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਬਾਚ ਰਾਧੇ ਸੋ","roman":"Kaanh joo baach raadhe so","meaning_en":"Kanh said to Radha:","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[743],"number_text":"੭੪੩।","page":454,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੋਹਿਯੋ ਹਉ ਤੇਰੋ ਸਖੀ ਚਲਿਬੋ ਪਿਖਿ ਮੋਹਿਯੋ ਸੁ ਹਉ ਦ੍ਰਿਗ ਪੇਖਤ ਤੇਰੇ।","roman":"Mohiyo hau tero sakhee chalibo pikhi mohiyo su hau drig pekhat tere |","meaning_en":"'Friend, I am enchanted seeing your walk; I am enchanted gazing at your eyes;","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੋਹਿ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਅਲਕੈ ਤੁਮਰੀ ਪਿਖਿ ਜਾਤ ਗਯੋ ਤਜਿ ਯਾ ਨਹੀ ਡੇਰੇ।","roman":"Mohi rahiyo alkai tumree pikhi jaat gayo taji yaa nahee dere |","meaning_en":"I am enchanted seeing your locks of hair; I cannot leave and go from this place;","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਡੇਰੇ: 'dwelling, place'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੋਹਿ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਤੁਹਿ ਅੰਗ ਨਿਹਾਰਤ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਬਢੀ ਤਿਹ ਤੇ ਮਨ ਮੇਰੇ।","roman":"Mohi rahiyo tuhi ang nihaarat preeti badhee tih te man mere |","meaning_en":"I am enchanted beholding your limbs; from that, love has grown in my heart;","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੋਹਿ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਮੁਖ ਤੇਰੋ ਨਿਹਾਰਤ ਜਿਉ ਗਨ ਚੰਦ ਚਕੋਰਨ ਹੇਰੇ। ੭੪੩।","roman":"Mohi rahiyo mukh tero nihaarat jiu gan chand chakoran here | 743 |","meaning_en":"I am enchanted gazing at your face, as flocks of chakor birds gaze at the moon.'","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[744],"number_text":"੭੪੪।","page":454,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਤੇ ਨ ਮਾਨ ਕਰੋ ਸਜਨੀ ਮੁਹਿ ਸੰਗ ਚਲੋ ਉਠ ਕੈ ਅਬ ਹੀ।","roman":"Taa te na maan karo sajnee muhi sang chalo uth kai ab hee |","meaning_en":"'So do not sulk, friend; rise and come with me right now;","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਮਰੀ ਤੁਮ ਸੋ ਸਖੀ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਘਨੀ ਕੁਪਿ ਬਾਤ ਕਹੋ ਤਜਿ ਕੈ ਸਬ ਹੀ।","roman":"Hamree tum so sakhee preeti ghanee kupi baat kaho taji kai sab hee |","meaning_en":"friend, my love for you is great; leave everything that you say in anger;","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਹ ਤੇ ਇਹ ਛੁਦ੍ਰਨ ਬਾਤ ਕੀ ਰੀਤਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਨ ਅਰੀ ਤੁਮ ਕੋ ਫਬ ਹੀ।","roman":"Tih te ih chhudran baat kee reeti kahiyo na aree tum ko phab hee |","meaning_en":"so these petty ways of speaking, I say, do not become you, dear;","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਹ ਤੇ ਸੁਨ ਮੋ ਬਿਨਤੀ ਚਲੀਯੈ ਇਹ ਕਾਜ ਕੀਏ ਨ ਕਛੂ ਲਭ ਹੀ। ੭੪੪।","roman":"Tih te sun mo bintee chaleeyai ih kaaj kee'e na kachhoo labh hee | 744 |","meaning_en":"so listen to my plea and come; nothing is gained by doing this.'","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[745],"number_text":"੭੪੫।","page":454,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਜਬ ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਕਰੀ ਬਿਨਤੀ ਤਬ ਹੀ ਮਨ ਰੰਚ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਸੋਊ ਮਾਨੀ।","roman":"Ati hee jab kaanh karee bintee tab hee man ranch treeyaa so'oo maanee |","meaning_en":"When Kanh pleaded so much, then the woman relented a little in her heart;","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੂਰ ਕਰੀ ਮਨ ਕੀ ਗਨਤੀ ਜਬ ਹੀ ਹਰਿ ਕੀ ਤਿਨ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਪਛਾਨੀ।","roman":"Door karee man kee gantee jab hee hari kee tin preeti pachhaanee |","meaning_en":"she put away the reckonings of her mind as soon as she recognised Krishna's love;","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਉ ਇਮ ਉਤਰ ਦੇਤ ਭਈ ਜੋਊ ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ ਮਹਿ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਨ ਰਾਨੀ।","roman":"Tau im utar det bhaee jo'oo sundartaa mahi treeyan raanee |","meaning_en":"then she who is queen among women in beauty answered thus;","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਯਾਗ ਦਈ ਦੁਚਿਤਈ ਮਨ ਕੀ ਹਰਿ ਸੋ ਰਸ ਬਾਤਨ ਸੋ ਨਿਜ ਕਾਨੀ। ੭੪੫।","roman":"Tyaag daee duchitaee man kee hari so ras baatan so nij kaanee | 745 |","meaning_en":"she gave up the doubt of her heart, (won) by Krishna's loving words to her own ears.","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਿਜ ਕਾਨੀ: read as 'in her own ears'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[746],"number_text":"੭੪੬।","page":454,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੋਹਿ ਕਹੋ ਚਲੀਯੈ ਹਮਰੇ ਸੰਗ ਜਾਨਤ ਹੋ ਰਸ ਸਾਥ ਛਰੋਗੇ।","roman":"Mohi kaho chaleeyai hamre sang jaanat ho ras saath chharoge |","meaning_en":"'You tell me, \"Come with me\"; I know you will deceive me in love;","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਸ ਬਿਖੈ ਹਮ ਕੋ ਸੰਗ ਲੈ ਸਖੀ ਜਾਨਤ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਸੰਗ ਅਰੋਗੇ।","roman":"Raas bikhai ham ko sang lai sakhee jaanat gvaarni sang aroge |","meaning_en":"taking me with you to the Ras, friend, I know you will get entangled with the gopis;","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਰੋਗੇ: read as 'get entangled'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਉ ਨਹੀ ਹਾਰਿ ਹਉ ਪੈ ਤੁਮਤੇ ਤੁਮ ਹੀ ਹਮ ਤੇ ਹਰਿ ਹਾਰਿ ਪਰੋਗੇ।","roman":"Hau nahee haari hau pai tumte tum hee ham te hari haari paroge |","meaning_en":"I will not be beaten by you; it is you, Krishna, who will be beaten by me;","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਏਕ ਨ ਜਾਨਤ ਕੁੰਜ ਗਲੀਨ ਲਵਾਇ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਕਛੁ ਕਾਜੁ ਕਰੋਗੇ। ੭੪੬।","roman":"Ek na jaanat kunj galeen lavaai kahiyo kachhu kaaju karoge | 746 |","meaning_en":"no one knows what deed you will do, leading me into the arbour lanes,' she said.","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Line read loosely; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[747],"number_text":"੭੪੭।","page":454,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਅਤਿ ਜੋ ਹਰਿ ਕੇ ਰਸ ਭੀਤਰ ਭੀਨੀ।","roman":"Brikhbhaan sutaa kabi syaam kahai ati jo hari ke ras bheetar bheenee |","meaning_en":"Brikhbhan's daughter, says the poet Shyam, who was deeply steeped in Krishna's love —","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੀ ਬ੍ਰਿਜਨਾਥ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਹਸਿ ਕੈ ਛਬਿ ਦਾਤਨ ਕੀ ਅਤਿ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਚੀਨੀ।","roman":"Ree brijnaath kahiyo hasi kai chhabi daatan kee ati sundar cheenee |","meaning_en":"'Oh!' — the lord of Braj spoke, laughing; she saw the very beautiful splendour of his teeth;","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Line read loosely; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਛਬਿ ਕੀ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਉਪਮਾ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਜੁ ਭਈ ਕਬਿ ਕੇ ਸੋਊ ਕੀਨੀ।","roman":"Taa chhabi kee ati hee upmaa man mai ju bhaee kabi ke so'oo keenee |","meaning_en":"the likeness of that splendour, as it came into the poet's mind, he made thus:","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਉ ਘਨ ਬੀਚ ਲਸੈ ਚਪਲਾ ਤਿਹ ਕੋ ਠਗ ਕੈ ਠਗਨੀ ਠਗ ਲੀਨੀ। ੭੪੭।","roman":"Jiu ghan beech lasai chaplaa tih ko thag kai thagnee thag leenee | 747 |","meaning_en":"as lightning flashes in a cloud; the cheating woman has cheated the cheat.","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[748],"number_text":"੭੪੮।","page":454,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਅਤਿ ਜੋ ਹਰਿ ਕੇ ਰਸ ਭੀਤਰ ਭੀਨੀ।","roman":"Brikhbhaan sutaa kabi syaam kahai ati jo hari ke ras bheetar bheenee |","meaning_en":"Brikhbhan's daughter, says the poet Shyam, who was deeply steeped in Krishna's love —","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੀਚ ਹੁਲਾਸ ਬਢਿਯੋ ਮਨ ਕੈ ਜਬ ਕਾਨ ਕੀ ਬਾਤ ਸਭੈ ਮਨਿ ਲੀਨੀ।","roman":"Beech hulaas badhiyo man kai jab kaan kee baat sabhai mani leenee |","meaning_en":"joy grew in her heart when she took all of Kanh's words to heart;","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੁੰਜ ਗਲੀਨ ਮੈ ਖੇਲਹਿੰਗੇ ਹਰਿ ਕੇ ਤਿਨ ਸੰਗ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਸੋਊ ਕੀਨੀ।","roman":"Kunj galeen mai khelhinge hari ke tin sang kahiyo so'oo keenee |","meaning_en":"'We will play in the arbour lanes,' she said with Krishna, and did so;","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਹਸਿ ਬਾਤ ਨਿਸੰਗ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਮਨ ਕੀ ਦੁਚਿਤਾਈ ਸਭ ਹੀ ਤਜਿ ਦੀਨੀ। ੭੪੮।","roman":"Yau hasi baat nisang kahiyo man kee duchitaaee sabh hee taji deenee | 748 |","meaning_en":"thus she spoke smiling, without hesitation, and gave up all the doubt of her heart.","page":454,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[749],"number_text":"੭੪੯।","page":455,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦੋਊ ਜਉ ਹਸਿ ਬਾਤਨ ਸੰਗ ਢਰੇ ਤੁ ਹੁਲਾਸ ਬਿਲਾਸ ਬਢੇ ਸਗਰੇ।","roman":"Do'oo jau hasi baatan sang dhare tu hulaas bilaas badhe sagre |","meaning_en":"When both melted in laughing talk, all joy and delight increased;","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਸਿ ਕੰਠ ਲਗਾਇ ਲਈ ਲਲਨਾ ਗਹਿ ਗਾੜੇ ਅਨੰਗ ਤੇ ਅੰਕ ਭਰੇ।","roman":"Hasi kanth lagaai laee lalnaa gahi gaare anang te ank bhare |","meaning_en":"laughing, he drew the beloved to his breast, holding her tight in an embrace through love's force;","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਨੰਗ: 'the bodiless one', Kamdev; read as 'through passion'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਰਕੀ ਹੈ ਤਨੀ ਦਰਕੀ ਅੰਗੀਆ ਗਰ ਮਾਲ ਤੇ ਟੂਟ ਕੈ ਲਾਲ ਪਰੇ।","roman":"Tarkee hai tanee darkee angeeaa gar maal te toot kai laal pare |","meaning_en":"the strings snapped, the bodice tore, and rubies broke from the necklace and fell;","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੀਯ ਕੇ ਮਿਲਏ ਤ੍ਰੀਯ ਕੇ ਹੀਯ ਤੇ ਅੰਗਰਾ ਬਿਰਹਾਗਨਿ ਕੇ ਨਿਕਰੇ। ੭੪੯।","roman":"Peey ke milae treey ke heey te angraa birhaagni ke nikre | 749 |","meaning_en":"as the beloved met her, the embers of the fire of separation came out of the woman's heart.","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[750],"number_text":"੭੫੦।","page":455,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਰਿ ਰਾਧਿਕਾ ਸੰਗਿ ਚਲੇ ਬਨ ਲੈ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਮਨਿ ਆਨੰਦ ਪਾਯੋ।","roman":"Hari raadhikaa sangi chale ban lai kabi syaam kahai mani aanand paayo |","meaning_en":"Krishna went with Radhika into the forest, says the poet Shyam, and found joy in his heart;","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੁੰਜ ਗਲੀਨ ਮੈ ਕੇਲ ਕਰੇ ਮਨ ਕੋ ਸਭ ਸੋਕ ਹੁਤੋ ਬਿਸਰਾਯੋ।","roman":"Kunj galeen mai kel kare man ko sabh sok huto bisraayo |","meaning_en":"in the arbour lanes they played, and all the sorrow of heart there had been was forgotten;","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਕਥਾ ਕੌ ਕਿਧੌ ਜਗ ਮੈ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਸੁਕ ਆਦਿਕ ਗਾਇ ਸੁਨਾਯੋ।","roman":"Taahee kathaa kau kidhau jag mai man mai suk aadik gaai sunaayo |","meaning_en":"it is this story that Shukdev and others sang and recited in the world;","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁਕ: read as Shukdev, narrator of the Bhagavata; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋਊ ਸੁਨੈ ਸੋਊ ਰੀਝ ਰਹੈ ਜਿਹ ਕੇ ਸਭ ਹੀ ਧਰਿ ਮੈ ਜਸੁ ਛਾਯੋ। ੭੫੦।","roman":"Jo'oo sunai so'oo reejh rahai jih ke sabh hee dhari mai jasu chhaayo | 750 |","meaning_en":"whoever hears it is enraptured; its praise has spread over all the earth.","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਬਾਚ ਰਾਧੇ ਸੋ","gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਬਾਚ ਰਾਧੇ ਸੋ","roman":"Kaanh joo baach raadhe so","meaning_en":"Kanh said to Radha:","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[751],"number_text":"੭੫੧।","page":455,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਇਮ ਰਾਧਿਕਾ ਸੰਗਿ ਕਹੀ ਜਮੁਨਾ ਮੈ ਤਰੋ ਤੁਮ ਕੋ ਗਹਿ ਹੈ।","roman":"Hari joo im raadhikaa sangi kahee jamunaa mai taro tum ko gahi hai |","meaning_en":"Krishna said thus to Radhika: 'Swim in the Yamuna; I will catch you;","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਲ ਮੈ ਹਮ ਕੇਲ ਕਰੈ ਗੈ ਸੁਨੋ ਰਸ ਬਾਤ ਸਭੈ ਸੁ ਤਹਾ ਕਹਿ ਹੈ।","roman":"Jal mai ham kel karai gai suno ras baat sabhai su tahaa kahi hai |","meaning_en":"we will play in the water; listen, there we will say all words of love;","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਹ ਓਰ ਨਿਹਾਰ ਬਧੂ ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਕੀ ਲਲਚਾਇ ਮਨੈ ਪਿਖਿਬੋ ਚਹਿ ਹੈ।","roman":"Jih or nihaar badhoo brij kee lalchaai manai pikhibo chahi hai |","meaning_en":"the women of Braj, looking that way, will long in their hearts to watch;","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਹੁਚੈਗੀ ਨਹਿ ਤਹ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਏ ਹਮ ਹੂੰ ਤੁਮ ਰੀਝਤ ਹਾਰਹਿ ਹੈ। ੭੫੧।","roman":"Pahuchaigee nahi tah gvaarni e ham hoon tum reejhat haarhi hai | 751 |","meaning_en":"these gopis will not reach there; you and I will lose ourselves in delight.'","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹਾਰਹਿ: read as 'be overcome, lose ourselves'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[752],"number_text":"੭੫੨।","page":455,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਹਰਿ ਕੇ ਮੁਖ ਤੇ ਜਲ ਪੈਠਨ ਕੀ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਸੁਨਿ ਪਾਈ।","roman":"Brikhbhaan sutaa hari ke mukh te jal paithan kee bateeyaa suni paaee |","meaning_en":"Brikhbhan's daughter heard from Krishna's mouth the words about entering the water;","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਾਇ ਕੈ ਜਾਇ ਪਰੀ ਸਰ ਮੈ ਕਰਿ ਕੈ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਬ੍ਰਿਜਨਾਥਿ ਬਡਾਈ।","roman":"Dhaai kai jaai paree sar mai kari kai ati hee brijnaathi badaaee |","meaning_en":"she ran and plunged into the pool, greatly praising the lord of Braj;","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਕੇ ਪਾਛੈ ਤੇ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਪਰੇ ਕਬਿ ਕੇ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਉਪਮਾ ਇਹ ਆਈ।","roman":"Taahee ke paachhai te syaam pare kabi ke man mai upmaa ih aaee |","meaning_en":"after her Shyam plunged in; this likeness came into the poet's mind:","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਨਹੁ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਜੂ ਬਾਜ ਪਰਿਯੋ ਪਿਖਿ ਕੈ ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਨਾਰਿ ਕੋ ਜਿਉ ਮੁਰਗਾਈ। ੭੫੨।","roman":"Maanhu syaam joo baaj pariyo pikhi kai brij naari ko jiu murgaaee | 752 |","meaning_en":"as if Shyam were a hawk swooping on seeing the woman of Braj as a waterfowl.","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮੁਰਗਾਈ: a water-bird (coot or diver)."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[753],"number_text":"੭੫੩।","page":455,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬ੍ਰਿਜਨਾਥ ਤਬੈ ਧਸਿ ਕੈ ਜਲਿ ਮੈ ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਨਾਰਿ ਸੋਊ ਤਬ ਜਾਇ ਗਹੀ।","roman":"Brijnaath tabai dhasi kai jali mai brij naari so'oo tab jaai gahee |","meaning_en":"Then the lord of Braj, plunging into the water, went and caught that woman of Braj;","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਰਿ ਕੋ ਤਨ ਭੇਟ ਹੁਲਾਸ ਬਢਿਯੋ ਗਿਨਤੀ ਮਨ ਕੀ ਜਲ ਭਾਤਿ ਬਹੀ।","roman":"Hari ko tan bhet hulaas badhiyo gintee man kee jal bhaati bahee |","meaning_en":"touching Krishna's body, her joy grew, and the reckonings of her mind flowed away like water;","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋਊ ਆਨੰਦ ਬੀਚ ਬਢਿਯੋ ਮਨ ਕੈ ਕਬਿ ਤਉ ਮੁਖ ਤੇ ਕਥਾ ਭਾਖਿ ਕਹੀ।","roman":"Jo'oo aanand beech badhiyo man kai kabi tau mukh te kathaa bhaakhi kahee |","meaning_en":"the joy that rose in her heart, the poet then told as a story from his mouth;","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਿਖਿਯੋ ਜਿਨ ਹੂੰ ਸੋਊ ਰੀਝ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਪਿਖਿ ਕੈ ਜਮੁਨਾ ਜਿਹ ਰੀਝ ਰਹੀ। ੭੫੩।","roman":"Pikhiyo jin hoon so'oo reejh rahiyo pikhi kai jamunaa jih reejh rahee | 753 |","meaning_en":"whoever saw it was enraptured; seeing it, the Yamuna herself was enraptured.","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[754],"number_text":"੭੫੪।","page":455,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਲ ਤੇ ਕਢਿ ਕੈ ਫਿਰਿ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨਿ ਸੋ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਫਿਰਿ ਰਾਸ ਮਚਾਯੋ।","roman":"Jal te kadhi kai phiri gvaarni so kabi syaam kahai phiri raas machaayo |","meaning_en":"Coming out of the water, says the poet Shyam, he again started the Ras with the gopis;","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਾਵਤ ਭੀ ਬ੍ਰਿਖਭਾਨ ਸੁਤਾ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਮਨ ਭੀਤਰ ਆਨੰਦ ਪਾਯੋ।","roman":"Gaavat bhee brikhbhaan sutaa ati hee man bheetar aanand paayo |","meaning_en":"Brikhbhan's daughter sang too, and found great joy in her heart;","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਨਾਰਿਨ ਸੋ ਮਿਲ ਕੈ ਬ੍ਰਿਜਨਾਥ ਜੂ ਸਾਰੰਗ ਮੈ ਇਕ ਤਾਨ ਬਸਾਯੋ।","roman":"Brij naarin so mil kai brijnaath joo saarang mai ik taan basaayo |","meaning_en":"joining with the women of Braj, the lord of Braj set a strain in raga Sarang;","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋ ਸੁਨ ਕੈ ਮ੍ਰਿਗ ਆਵਤ ਧਾਵਤ ਗ੍ਵਾਰਨੀਆ ਸੁਨ ਕੈ ਸੁਖੁ ਪਾਯੋ। ੭੫੪।","roman":"So sun kai mrig aavat dhaavat gvaarneeaa sun kai sukhu paayo | 754 |","meaning_en":"hearing it, the deer came running, and the gopis felt joy on hearing it.","page":455,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":456,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[755],"number_text":"੭੫੫।","page":456,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਤ੍ਰਹ ਸੈ ਪੈਤਾਲ ਮੈ ਕੀਨੀ ਕਥਾ ਸੁਧਾਰ।","roman":"Satrah sai paitaal mai keenee kathaa sudhaar |","meaning_en":"In (Samvat) seventeen hundred and forty-five this story was set in order;","page":456,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Samvat 1745 (about 1688 CE)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਚੂਕ ਹੋਇ ਜਹ ਤਹ ਸੁ ਕਬਿ ਲੀਜਹੁ ਸਕਲ ਸੁਧਾਰ। ੭੫੫।","roman":"Chook hoi jah tah su kabi leejhu sakal sudhaar | 755 |","meaning_en":"wherever there is any error, poets, please correct it all.","page":456,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[756],"number_text":"੭੫੬।","page":456,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਨਤਿ ਕਰੋ ਦੋਊ ਜੋਰਿ ਕਰਿ ਸੁਨੋ ਜਗਤ ਕੇ ਰਾਇ।","roman":"Binti karo do'oo jori kari suno jagat ke raai |","meaning_en":"I make my plea with both hands joined: listen, King of the world:","page":456,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੋ ਮਸਤਕ ਤ੍ਵ ਪਗ ਸਦਾ ਰਹੈ ਦਾਸ ਕੇ ਭਾਇ। ੭੫੬।","roman":"Mo mastak tva pag sadaa rahai daas ke bhaai | 756 |","meaning_en":"may my head ever rest at Your feet, in the spirit of a servant.","page":456,"meaning_status":"draft"}]}],"ending":{"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਤਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਦਸਮ ਸਿਕੰਧੇ ਪੁਰਾਣੇ ਬਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਨਾਟਕ ਗ੍ਰੰਥੇ ਕ੍ਰਿਸਨਾਵਤਾਰੇ","roman":"Iti sree dasam sikandhe puraane bachitr naatak granthe krisnaavtaare","meaning_en":"Here ends, in Sri Dasam Skandh Puran, in the book Bachittar Natak, in Krishnavtar,","page":456,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਸ ਮੰਡਲ ਬਰਨਨੰ ਧਿਆਇ ਸਮਾਪਤਮ ਸਤੁ ਸੁਭਮ ਸਤੁ।","roman":"Raas mandal barannan dhiaai samaaptam satu subham satu |","meaning_en":"the chapter describing the Ras Mandal (the circle of the dance). All is well.","page":456,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"'ਸਤੁ ਸੁਭਮ ਸਤੁ': conventional closing, 'may it be true and auspicious'."}],"page":456}});
